{"cklb_version":"1.0","title":"SCC Generated CKLB at: 2026-09-05T13:03:13","stigs":[{"stig_id":"IE_11_STIG","classification":"UNCLASSIFIED","display_name":"Microsoft Internet Explorer 11","stig_name":"Microsoft Internet Explorer 11 Security Technical Implementation Guide","rules":[{"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page 'Turn on certificate address mismatch warning' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings Criteria: If the value \"WarnOnBadCertRecving\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"id":"V-223015","title":"SRG-APP-000516"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59339","V-46475"],"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"This parameter warns users if the certificate being presented by the website is invalid. Since server certificates are used to validate the identity of the web server it is critical to warn the user of a potential issue with the certificate being presented by the web server. This setting aids to prevent spoofing attacks.","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516","group_id":"V-223015","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","rule_id":"SV-223015r961863","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"responsibility":"","rule_title":"The Internet Explorer warning about certificate address mismatch must be enforced.","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page 'Turn on certificate address mismatch warning' to 'Enabled'.  ","classification":"Unclassified","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Windows Components/Internet Explorer/Internet Control Panel/Security Page/Turn on certificate address mismatch warning)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:42100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Windows Components/Internet Explorer/Internet Control Panel/Security Page/Turn on certificate address mismatch warning\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:42100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Windows Components/Internet Explorer/Internet Control Panel/Security Page/Turn on certificate address mismatch warning\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'WarnOnBadCertRecving'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:42100 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Windows Components/Internet Explorer/Internet Control Panel/Security Page/Turn on certificate address mismatch warning\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings'\n                        : name equals 'WarnOnBadCertRecving'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223015r961863_rule","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:421"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI015-IE11","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4545368-6BF7-1014-8025-98CA964E5618","status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223015","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0"},{"stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223016","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000175","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Check for publisher's certificate revocation options should be enforced to ensure all PKI signed objects are validated.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-APP-000605","legacy_ids":["SV-59341","V-46477"],"check_content":"If the system is on the SIPRNet, this requirement is NA.\n\nOpen Internet Explorer.\nFrom the menu bar, select \"Tools\".\nFrom the \"Tools\" drop-down menu, select \"Internet Options\". From the \"Internet Options\" window, select the \"Advanced\" tab, from the \"Advanced\" tab window, scroll down to the \"Security\" category, and verify the \"Check for publisher's certificate revocation\" box is selected.\n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key:\n HKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\WinTrust\\Trust Providers\\Software Publishing Criteria\n\nIf the value \"State\" is \"REG_DWORD = 23C00\", this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000175","id":"V-223016"},"responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-000185"],"comments":null,"severity":"low","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223016r961038","rule_id_src":"SV-223016r961038_rule","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Check for publishers certificate revocation must be enforced.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ie:tst:22301601 (ntuser_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Check for publishers certificate revocation must be enforced.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ie:obj:22301601 (ntuser_object)\nObject Comment          : All user profiles: Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\WinTrust\\Trust Providers\\Software Publishing\\State\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\WinTrust\\Trust Providers\\Software Publishing'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'State'\nExclude Items If        : enabled equals 'false'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ie:ste:22301601 (ntuser_state)\nState Comment           : NTUSER Registry key type equals reg_dword and value equals 146432 (hex 23c00)\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '146432'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\WinTrust\\Trust Providers\\Software Publishing'\n                        : name equals 'State'\n                        : sid equals 'S-1-5-21-746496990-2641142201-3713043312-1001'\n                        : username equals 'SOT-WIN2K22-01\\degthat'\n                        : account_type equals 'local'\n                        : logged_on equals 'false'\n                        : days_since_last_logon equals '86'\n                        : enabled equals 'true'\n                        : date_modified equals '134331012880000000'\n                        : days_since_modified equals '1'\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Users\\degthat.WIN-95GFQRRMAS4\\ntuser.dat'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055469390000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '146432'\n","classification":"Unclassified","fix_text":"If the system is on the SIPRNet, this requirement is NA.\n\nOpen Internet Explorer.\nFrom the menu bar, select \"Tools\".\nFrom the \"Tools\" drop-down menu, select \"Internet Options\". From the \"Internet Options\" window, select the \"Advanced\" tab from the \"Advanced\" tab window, scroll down to the \"Security\" category, and select the \"Check for publisher's certificate revocation\" box.\n\nNote: Manual entry in the registry key:\n\nHKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Current Version\\WinTrust\\Trust Providers\\Software Publishing for the value \"State\", set to \"REG_DWORD = 23C00\", may first be required.","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Check for publishers certificate revocation must be enforced.","status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223016","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","uuid":"D45462A1-6BF7-1014-9DD9-9B81B77B52B9","potential_impacts":"","rule_version":"DTBI018-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ie:def:223016","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval2.xml"}},{"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:422","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI022-IE11","ia_controls":"","uuid":"D4547037-6BF7-1014-8504-F9A0F441F0FC","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223017","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Download signed ActiveX controls' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"The Download signed ActiveX controls property must be disallowed (Internet zone).","classification":"Unclassified","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Download signed ActiveX controls)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:42200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Download signed ActiveX controls\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:42200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Download signed ActiveX controls\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1001'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:42200 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Download signed ActiveX controls\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '1001'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223017r961089_rule","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223017r961089","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-001169"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59345","V-46481"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-223017","title":"SRG-APP-000209"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Download signed ActiveX controls' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box.  Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"1001\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Active X controls can contain potentially malicious code and must only be allowed to be downloaded from trusted sites. Signed code is better than unsigned code in that it may be easier to determine its author, but it is still potentially harmful, especially when coming from an untrusted zone. This policy setting allows you to manage whether users may download signed ActiveX controls from a page in the zone. If you enable this policy, users can download signed controls without user intervention. If you select Prompt in the drop-down box, users are queried whether to download controls signed by untrusted publishers. Code signed by trusted publishers is silently downloaded. If you disable the policy setting, signed controls cannot be downloaded.","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000209","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223017"},{"comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001169"],"responsibility":"","rule_id":"SV-223018r961089","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000209","group_id":"V-223018","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_tree":{"id":"V-223018","title":"SRG-APP-000209"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Download unsigned ActiveX controls' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"1004\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59347","V-46483"],"discussion":"Unsigned code is potentially harmful, especially when coming from an untrusted zone. This policy setting allows you to manage whether users may download unsigned ActiveX controls from the zone. If you enable this policy setting, users can run unsigned controls without user intervention. If you select \"Prompt\" in the drop-down box, users are queried to choose whether to allow the unsigned control to run. If you disable this policy setting, users cannot run unsigned controls. If you do not configure this policy setting, users cannot run unsigned controls.","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4547A79-6BF7-1014-8F5C-D342CFD4F5F9","group_id_src":"V-223018","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:423"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI023-IE11","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Download unsigned ActiveX controls)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:42300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Download unsigned ActiveX controls\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:42300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Download unsigned ActiveX controls\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1004'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:42300 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Download unsigned ActiveX controls\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '1004'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223018r961089_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"The Download unsigned ActiveX controls property must be disallowed (Internet zone).","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Download unsigned ActiveX controls' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box. ","reference_identifier":"4095","classification":"Unclassified"},{"group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223019","legacy_ids":["SV-59365","V-46501"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Initialize and script ActiveX controls not marked as safe' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"1201\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000210","id":"V-223019"},"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"ActiveX controls that are not marked safe for scripting should not be executed. Although this is not a complete security measure for a control to be marked safe for scripting, if a control is not marked safe, it should not be initialized and executed. This setting causes both unsafe and safe controls to be initialized and scripted, ignoring the Script ActiveX controls marked safe for scripting option. This increases the risk of malicious code being loaded and executed by the browser. If you enable this policy setting, ActiveX controls are run, loaded with parameters and scripted without setting object safety for untrusted data or scripts. If you disable this policy setting, ActiveX controls that cannot be made safe are not loaded with parameters or scripted. This setting is not recommended, except for secure and administered zones.","ccis":["CCI-001170"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223019r961092","severity":"medium","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Initialize and script ActiveX controls not marked as safe)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:42400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Initialize and script ActiveX controls not marked as safe\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:42400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Initialize and script ActiveX controls not marked as safe\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1201'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:42400 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Initialize and script ActiveX controls not marked as safe\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '1201'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223019r961092_rule","mitigation_control":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Initialize and script ActiveX controls not marked as safe' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"The Initialize and script ActiveX controls not marked as safe property must be disallowed (Internet zone).","classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"D45486F7-6BF7-1014-AEBF-8774C31AC097","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223019","mitigations":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:424","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI024-IE11","ia_controls":""},{"discussion":"Java applications could contain malicious code; sites located in this security zone are more likely to be hosted by malicious individuals. This policy setting allows you to manage permissions for Java applets. If you enable this policy setting, options can be chosen from the drop-down box. Use of the Custom permission will control permissions settings individually. Use of the Low Safety permission enables applets to perform all operations. Use of the Medium Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox (an area in memory outside of which the program cannot make calls), plus adds capabilities like scratch space (a safe and secure storage area on the client computer) and a user-controlled file I/O. Use of the High Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox. If you disable this policy setting, Java applets cannot run. If you do not configure this policy setting, the permission is set to High Safety.","security_override_guidance":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-223020","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable Java' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"1C00\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59371","V-46507"],"group_id":"V-223020","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","severity":"medium","rule_id":"SV-223020r960963","false_positives":"","responsibility":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"classification":"Unclassified","rule_title":"The Java permissions must be disallowed (Internet zone).","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable Java' from the drop-down box.  ","reference_identifier":"4095","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223020r960963_rule","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Java permissions)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:42600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Java permissions\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:42600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Java permissions\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1C00'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:42600 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Java permissions\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '1C00'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI031-IE11","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:426"},"mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223020","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4548FC4-6BF7-1014-9B82-E0B429C1271B"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Access data sources across domains)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:42700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Access data sources across domains\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:42700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Access data sources across domains\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1406'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:42700 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Access data sources across domains\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '1406'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223021r1117169_rule","mitigation_control":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Access data sources across domains' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Accessing data sources across domains must be disallowed (Internet zone).","classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"D45497E3-6BF7-1014-A1E3-C540EA9B4CF8","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223021","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:427","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI032-IE11","ia_controls":"","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000039","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223021","legacy_ids":["SV-59373","V-46509"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Access data sources across domains' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"1406\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"id":"V-223021","title":"SRG-APP-000039"},"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"The ability to access data zones across domains could cause the user to unknowingly access content hosted on an unauthorized server. Access to data sources across multiple domains must be controlled based upon the site being browsed. This policy setting allows you to manage whether Internet Explorer can access data from another security zone using the Microsoft XML Parser (MSXML) or ActiveX Data Objects (ADO).","ccis":["CCI-001414"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","rule_id":"SV-223021r1117169","false_positives":"","severity":"medium"},{"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:428","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI036-IE11","ia_controls":"","uuid":"D454AE66-6BF7-1014-A071-FBEF9E907C77","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-223022","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Allow drag and drop or copy and paste files' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Functionality to drag and drop or copy and paste files must be disallowed (Internet zone).","classification":"Unclassified","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow drag and drop or copy and paste files)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:42800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow drag and drop or copy and paste files\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:42800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow drag and drop or copy and paste files\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1802'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:42800 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow drag and drop or copy and paste files\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '1802'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223022r960963_rule","rule_id":"SV-223022r960963","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59375","V-46511"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Allow drag and drop or copy and paste files' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value for \"1802\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223022"},"discussion":"Content hosted on sites located in the Internet zone are likely to contain malicious payloads and therefore this feature should be blocked for this zone. Drag and drop or copy and paste files must have a level of protection based upon the site being accessed.","security_override_guidance":"","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223022"},{"third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Launching applications and files in an IFRAME)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:42900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Launching applications and files in an IFRAME\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:42900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Launching applications and files in an IFRAME\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1804'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:42900 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Launching applications and files in an IFRAME\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '1804'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223023r960963_rule","rule_title":"Launching programs and files in IFRAME must be disallowed (Internet zone).","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Launching applications and files in an IFRAME' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.  ","classification":"Unclassified","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D454B9A7-6BF7-1014-88A4-A2D643E58C4E","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223023","mitigations":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:429"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI038-IE11","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","group_id":"V-223023","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_tree":{"id":"V-223023","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Launching applications and files in an IFRAME' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"1804\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59377","V-46513"],"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"This policy setting allows you to manage whether applications may be run and files may be downloaded from an IFRAME reference in the HTML of the pages in this zone. Launching of programs in IFRAME must have a level of protection based upon the site being accessed. If you enable this policy setting, applications can run and files can be downloaded from IFRAMEs on the pages in this zone without user intervention. If you disable this setting, users are prevented from running applications and downloading files from IFRAMEs on the pages in this zone.","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223023r960963","severity":"medium"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Navigate windows and frames across different domains)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:43000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Navigate windows and frames across different domains\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:43000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Navigate windows and frames across different domains\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1607'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:43000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Navigate windows and frames across different domains\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '1607'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223024r1117169_rule","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Navigate windows and frames across different domains' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Navigating windows and frames across different domains must be disallowed (Internet zone).","classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"D454C464-6BF7-1014-99A7-9EC64F0A3D2E","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-223024","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:430"},"rule_version":"DTBI039-IE11","ia_controls":"","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000039","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223024","legacy_ids":["SV-59379","V-46515"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-223024","title":"SRG-APP-000039"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Navigate windows and frames across different domains' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\InternetSettings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"1607\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","discussion":"Frames that navigate across different domains are a security concern, because the user may think they are accessing pages on one site while they are actually accessing pages on another site. It is possible that a website hosting malicious content could use this feature in a manner similar to cross-site scripting (XSS). This policy setting allows you to manage the opening of sub-frames and access of applications across different domains.","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-001414"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","rule_id":"SV-223024r1117169","false_positives":"","severity":"medium"},{"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Userdata persistence must have a level of protection based upon the site being accessed. It is possible for sites hosting malicious content to exploit this feature as part of an attack against visitors browsing the site. This policy setting allows you to manage the preservation of information in the browser's history, in Favorites, in an XML store, or directly within a web page saved to disk. When a user returns to a persisted page, the state of the page can be restored if this policy setting is not appropriately configured. ","legacy_ids":["SV-59381","V-46517"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000231","id":"V-223025"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Userdata persistence' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"1606\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223025","group_title":"SRG-APP-000231","documentable":"false","severity":"medium","rule_id":"SV-223025r961128","false_positives":"","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-001199"],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Userdata persistence' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","rule_title":"Userdata persistence must be disallowed (Internet zone).","rule_id_src":"SV-223025r961128_rule","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Userdata persistence)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:43100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Userdata persistence\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:43100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Userdata persistence\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1606'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:43100 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Userdata persistence\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '1606'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_version":"DTBI042-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:431"},"status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223025","mitigations":"","uuid":"D454CE7D-6BF7-1014-AA38-FFE94CC40DC8","potential_impacts":""},{"rule_version":"DTBI044-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:432"},"status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223026","mitigations":"","uuid":"D454D716-6BF7-1014-8C6D-96B5E90C045E","potential_impacts":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Allow cut, copy or paste operations from the clipboard via script' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","rule_title":"Clipboard operations via script must be disallowed (Internet zone).","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223026r960963_rule","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow cut, copy, or paste operations from the clipboard via script)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:43200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow cut, copy, or paste operations from the clipboard via script\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:43200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow cut, copy, or paste operations from the clipboard via script\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1407'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:43200 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow cut, copy, or paste operations from the clipboard via script\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '1407'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","severity":"medium","rule_id":"SV-223026r960963","false_positives":"","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"comments":null,"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"A malicious script could use the clipboard in an undesirable manner, for example, if the user had recently copied confidential information to the clipboard while editing a document, a malicious script could harvest that information. It might be possible to exploit other vulnerabilities in order to send the harvested data to the attacker. Allow paste operations via script must have a level of protection based upon the site being accessed.","legacy_ids":["SV-59385","V-46521"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-223026","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Allow cut, copy or paste operations from the clipboard via script' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"1407\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223026","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false"},{"severity":"medium","rule_id":"SV-223027r1043178","false_positives":"","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-001184"],"comments":null,"discussion":"Users could submit credentials to servers operated by malicious individuals who could then attempt to connect to legitimate servers with those captured credentials. Care must be taken with user credentials, automatic logon performance, and how default Windows credentials are passed to the websites. This policy setting allows management of settings for logon options. If you enable this policy setting, you can choose from varying logon options. âAnonymous logonâ disables HTTP authentication and uses the guest account only for the Common Internet File System (CIFS) protocol. âPrompt for user name and passwordâ queries users for user IDs and passwords. After a user is queried, these values can be used silently for the remainder of the session. âAutomatic logon only in Intranet zoneâ queries users for user IDs and passwords in other zones. After a user is queried, these values can be used silently for the remainder of the session. âAutomatic logon with current user name and passwordâ attempts logon using Windows NT Challenge Response. If Windows NT Challenge Response is supported by the server, the logon uses the user's network user name and password for login. If Windows NT Challenge Response is not supported by the server, the user is queried to provide the user name and password. If you disable this policy setting, logon is set to âAutomatic logon only in Intranet zoneâ. If you do not configure this policy setting, logon is set to âAutomatic logon only in Intranet zoneâ. The most secure option is to configure this setting to âEnabledâ; âAnonymous logonâ, but configuring this setting to âEnabledâ; âPrompt for user name and passwordâ, provides a reasonable balance between security and usability.","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59387","V-46523"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Logon options' must be 'Enabled', and 'Prompt for user name and password' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"1A00\" is REG_DWORD = 65536 (decimal), this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000219","id":"V-223027"},"stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223027","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000219","rule_version":"DTBI046-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:433","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223027","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"D454E0C5-6BF7-1014-8E05-E167D2AE4E32","potential_impacts":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Logon options' to 'Enabled', and select 'Prompt for user name and password' from the drop-down box.  ","rule_title":"Logon options must be configured to prompt (Internet zone).","rule_id_src":"SV-223027r1043178_rule","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Logon options)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:43300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Logon options\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:43300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Logon options\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1A00'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:43300 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Logon options\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '65536'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '1A00'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '65536'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":""},{"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","rule_id":"SV-223028r960963","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223028","legacy_ids":["SV-59389","V-46525"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Intranet Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' must be 'Enabled', and 'High Safety' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\1 Criteria: If the value \"1C00\" is REG_DWORD = 65536, (Decimal), this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223028"},"discussion":"Java applications could contain malicious code. This policy setting allows you to manage permissions for Java applets. If you enable this policy setting, options can be chosen from the drop-down box. Use of the Custom permission will control permissions settings individually. Use of the Low Safety permission enables applets to perform all operations. Use of the Medium Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox (an area in memory outside of which the program cannot make calls), plus adds capabilities like scratch space (a safe and secure storage area on the client computer) and a user-controlled file I/O. Use of the High Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox. If you disable this policy setting, Java applets cannot run. If you do not configure this policy setting, the permission is set to High Safety.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"D454E9E0-6BF7-1014-A4C7-FB2C5975E28C","potential_impacts":"","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223028","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:434"},"rule_version":"DTBI061-IE11","ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Intranet Zone\\Java permissions)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:43400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Intranet Zone\\Java permissions\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:43400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Intranet Zone\\Java permissions\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\1'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1C00'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:43400 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Intranet Zone\\Java permissions\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '65536'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\1'\n                        : name equals '1C00'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '65536'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_id_src":"SV-223028r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Intranet Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' to 'Enabled', and select 'High Safety' from the drop-down box.   ","rule_title":"Java permissions must be configured with High Safety (Intranet zone).","classification":"Unclassified"},{"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Intranet Zone 'Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls' to 'Enabled' and select 'Disable' in the drop-down box.   ","rule_title":"Anti-Malware programs against ActiveX controls must be run for the Intranet zone.","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223029r961086_rule","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Intranet Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:56600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Intranet Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:56600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Intranet Zone\\Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\1'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '270C'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:56600 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Intranet Zone\\Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\1'\n                        : name equals '270C'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","rule_version":"DTBI062-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:566","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223029","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"D454F687-6BF7-1014-9151-E4A9A158E0D1","potential_impacts":"","discussion":"This policy setting determines whether Internet Explorer runs Anti-Malware programs against ActiveX controls, to check if they're safe to load on pages.      If you enable this policy setting, Internet Explorer won't check with your Anti-Malware program to see if it's safe to create an instance of the ActiveX control. If you disable this policy setting, Internet Explorer always checks with your Anti-Malware program to see if it's safe to create an instance of the ActiveX control. If you don't configure this policy setting, Internet Explorer won't check with your Anti-Malware program to see if it's safe to create an instance of the ActiveX control. Users can turn this behavior on or off, using Internet Explorer Security settings.","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59865","V-46999"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Intranet Zone 'Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls' must be 'Enabled' and 'Disable' selected in the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\1  Criteria: If the value \"270C\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000207","id":"V-223029"},"stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223029","group_title":"SRG-APP-000207","documentable":"false","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223029r961086","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-001662"],"comments":null},{"comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"responsibility":"","rule_id":"SV-223030r960963","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","group_id":"V-223030","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223030"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Trusted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' must be 'Enabled', and 'High Safety' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\2 Criteria: If the value \"1C00\" is REG_DWORD = 65536, (Decimal), this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59407","V-46543"],"discussion":"Java applications could contain malicious code. This policy setting allows you to manage permissions for Java applets. If you enable this policy setting, options can be chosen from the drop-down box. Use of the Custom permission will control permissions settings individually. Use of the Low Safety permission enables applets to perform all operations. Use of the Medium Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox (an area in memory outside of which the program cannot make calls), plus adds capabilities like scratch space (a safe and secure storage area on the client computer) and a user-controlled file I/O. Use of the High Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox. If you disable this policy setting, Java applets cannot run. If you do not configure this policy setting, the permission is set to High Safety","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D455062A-6BF7-1014-AEF0-BD91A0617EF6","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223030","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:435","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI091-IE11","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Trusted Sites Zone\\Java permissions)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:43500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Trusted Sites Zone\\Java permissions\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:43500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Trusted Sites Zone\\Java permissions\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1C00'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:43500 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Trusted Sites Zone\\Java permissions\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '65536'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\2'\n                        : name equals '1C00'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '65536'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_id_src":"SV-223030r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Java permissions must be configured with High Safety (Trusted Sites zone).","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Trusted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' to 'Enabled', and select 'High Safety' from the drop-down box.","reference_identifier":"4095","classification":"Unclassified"},{"discussion":"This policy setting determines whether Internet Explorer runs Anti-Malware programs against ActiveX controls, to check if they're safe to load on pages.      If you enable this policy setting, Internet Explorer won't check with your Anti-Malware program to see if it's safe to create an instance of the ActiveX control. If you disable this policy setting, Internet Explorer always checks with your Anti-Malware program to see if it's safe to create an instance of the ActiveX control. If you don't configure this policy setting, Internet Explorer won't check with your Anti-Malware program to see if it's safe to create an instance of the ActiveX control. Users can turn this behavior on or off, using Internet Explorer Security settings.","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59875","V-47009"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-223031","title":"SRG-APP-000207"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Trusted Sites Zone 'Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls' must be 'Enabled' and 'Disable' selected in the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\2  Criteria: If the value \"270C\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223031","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000207","severity":"medium","rule_id":"SV-223031r961086","false_positives":"","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-001662"],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Trusted Sites Zone 'Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls' to 'Enabled' and select 'Disable' in the drop-down box.   ","rule_title":"Anti-Malware programs against ActiveX controls must be run for the Trusted Sites zone.","rule_id_src":"SV-223031r961086_rule","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Trusted Sites Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:56900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Trusted Sites Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:56900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Trusted Sites Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '270C'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:56900 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Trusted Sites Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\2'\n                        : name equals '270C'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_version":"DTBI092-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:569"},"weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223031","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"D4551175-6BF7-1014-8B51-EBC5BEFA22E0","potential_impacts":""},{"fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel-&gt; Security Page-&gt; Internet Zone 'Enable dragging of content from different domains within a window' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disabled' from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Dragging of content from different domains within a window must be disallowed (Internet zone).","classification":"Unclassified","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Enable dragging of content from different domains within a window)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:54900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Enable dragging of content from different domains within a window\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:54900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Enable dragging of content from different domains within a window\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '2708'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:54900 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Enable dragging of content from different domains within a window\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '2708'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_id_src":"SV-223032r1117169_rule","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:549","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI1000-IE11","ia_controls":"","uuid":"D4551BEC-6BF7-1014-B9A1-86C9A0343AE6","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-223032","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","legacy_ids":["SV-59409","V-46545"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-223032","title":"SRG-APP-000039"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel-&gt; Security Page-&gt; Internet Zone 'Enable dragging of content from different domains within a window' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disabled' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"2708\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","discussion":"This policy setting allows you to set options for dragging content from one domain to a different domain when the source and destination are in the same window. If you enable this policy setting, users can drag content from one domain to a different domain when the source and destination are in the same window. Users cannot change this setting. If you disable this policy setting, users cannot drag content from one domain to a different domain when the source and destination are in the same window. Users cannot change this setting in the Internet Options dialog box. If you do not configure this policy setting, users cannot drag content from one domain to a different domain when the source and destination are in the same window. Users can change this setting in the Internet Options dialog box.","security_override_guidance":"","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000039","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223032","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223032r1117169","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-001414"],"comments":null,"responsibility":""},{"ccis":["CCI-001414"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223033r1117169","severity":"medium","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000039","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223033","legacy_ids":["SV-59411","V-46547"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000039","id":"V-223033"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel-&gt; Security Page-&gt; Restricted Sites Zone 'Enable dragging of content from different domains across windows' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disabled' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"2709\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"This policy setting allows you to set options for dragging content from one domain to a different domain when the source and destination are in different windows. If you enable this policy setting, users can drag content from one domain to a different domain when the source and destination are in different windows. Users cannot change this setting. If you enable this policy setting, users cannot drag content from one domain to a different domain when both the source and destination are in different windows. Users cannot change this setting. If you do not configure this policy setting, users cannot drag content from one domain to a different domain when the source and destination are in different windows. Users can change this setting in the Internet Options dialog box.","uuid":"D4552619-6BF7-1014-BACA-847FDF188086","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223033","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:548","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI1005-IE11","ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Enable dragging of content from different domains across windows)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:54800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Enable dragging of content from different domains across windows\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:54800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Enable dragging of content from different domains across windows\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '2709'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:54800 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Enable dragging of content from different domains across windows\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '2709'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223033r1117169_rule","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel-&gt; Security Page-&gt; Restricted Sites Zone 'Enable dragging of content from different domains across windows' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disabled' from the drop-down box.   ","rule_title":"Dragging of content from different domains across windows must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","classification":"Unclassified"},{"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:535"},"rule_version":"DTBI1010-IE11","ia_controls":"","uuid":"D455303B-6BF7-1014-8FB8-A656E0FB4FBC","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223034","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Restrict ActiveX Install -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' to 'Enabled'.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Internet Explorer Processes Restrict ActiveX Install must be enforced (Explorer).","classification":"Unclassified","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Restrict ActiveX Install\\Internet Explorer Processes must be Enabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:53500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Restrict ActiveX Install\\Internet Explorer Processes must be Enabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:53500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Restrict ActiveX Install\\Internet Explorer Processes must be Enabled\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_RESTRICT_ACTIVEXINSTALL'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'explorer.exe'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:53500 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Restrict ActiveX Install\\Internet Explorer Processes must be Enabled\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_RESTRICT_ACTIVEXINSTALL'\n                        : name equals 'explorer.exe'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_id_src":"SV-223034r960921_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-223034r960921","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-001695"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59413","V-46549"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-223034","title":"SRG-APP-000112"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Restrict ActiveX Install -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_RESTRICT_ACTIVEXINSTALL   Criteria: If the value \"explorer.exe\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Users often choose to install software such as ActiveX controls that are not permitted by their organization's security policy. Such software can pose significant security and privacy risks to networks. This policy setting enables blocking of ActiveX control installation prompts for Internet Explorer processes. If you enable this policy setting, prompts for ActiveX control installations will be blocked for Internet Explorer processes. If you disable this policy setting, prompts for ActiveX control installations will not be blocked and these prompts will be displayed to users. If you do not configure this policy setting, the user's preference will be used to determine whether to block ActiveX control installations for Internet Explorer processes.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000112","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223034"},{"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:536","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI1020-IE11","ia_controls":"","uuid":"D4553E7B-6BF7-1014-91A