icy. Such software can pose significant security and privacy risks to networks. This policy setting enables blocking of ActiveX control installation prompts for Internet Explorer processes. If you enable this policy setting, prompts for ActiveX control installations will be blocked for Internet Explorer processes. If you disable this policy setting, prompts for ActiveX control installations will not be blocked and these prompts will be displayed to users. If you do not configure this policy setting, the user's preference will be used to determine whether to block ActiveX control installations for Internet Explorer processes.","security_override_guidance":"","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000112","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223035"},{"rule_version":"DTBI1025-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:550"},"status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223036","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","uuid":"D455490C-6BF7-1014-ABFE-93F455A0105C","potential_impacts":"","classification":"Unclassified","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel-&gt; Security Page-&gt; Restricted Sites Zone 'Enable dragging of content from different domains within a window' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disabled' from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Dragging of content from different domains within a window must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223036r1117169_rule","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Windows Components/Internet Explorer/Internet Control Panel/Security Page/Restricted Sites Zone/Enable dragging of content from different domains within a window)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:55000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Windows Components/Internet Explorer/Internet Control Panel/Security Page/Restricted Sites Zone/Enable dragging of content from different domains within a window\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:55000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Windows Components/Internet Explorer/Internet Control Panel/Security Page/Restricted Sites Zone/Enable dragging of content from different domains within a window\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '2708'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:55000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Windows Components/Internet Explorer/Internet Control Panel/Security Page/Restricted Sites Zone/Enable dragging of content from different domains within a window\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '2708'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223036r1117169","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-001414"],"comments":null,"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"This policy setting allows you to set options for dragging content from one domain to a different domain when the source and destination are in the same window. If you enable this policy setting, users can drag content from one domain to a different domain when the source and destination are in the same window. Users cannot change this setting. If you disable this policy setting, users cannot drag content from one domain to a different domain when the source and destination are in the same window. Users cannot change this setting in the Internet Options dialog box. If you do not configure this policy setting, users cannot drag content from one domain to a different domain when the source and destination are in the same window. Users can change this setting in the Internet Options dialog box.","legacy_ids":["SV-59419","V-46555"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel-&gt; Security Page-&gt; Restricted Sites Zone 'Enable dragging of content from different domains within a window' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disabled' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"2708\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000039","id":"V-223036"},"stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223036","group_title":"SRG-APP-000039","documentable":"false"},{"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI1046-IE11","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:565","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223037","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D455531D-6BF7-1014-960E-B5B274DF88D1","classification":"Unclassified","rule_title":"Anti-Malware programs against ActiveX controls must be run for the Internet zone.","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone 'Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls' to 'Enabled' and select 'Disable' in the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223037r961086_rule","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:56500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:56500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '270C'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:56500 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '270C'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","severity":"medium","rule_id":"SV-223037r961086","false_positives":"","responsibility":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001662"],"discussion":"This policy setting determines whether Internet Explorer runs Anti-Malware programs against ActiveX controls, to check if they're safe to load on pages.      If you enable this policy setting, Internet Explorer won't check with your Anti-Malware program to see if it's safe to create an instance of the ActiveX control. If you disable this policy setting, Internet Explorer always checks with your Anti-Malware program to see if it's safe to create an instance of the ActiveX control. If you don't configure this policy setting, Internet Explorer always checks with your Anti-Malware program to see if it's safe to create an instance of the ActiveX control. Users can turn this behavior on or off, using Internet Explorer Security settings.","security_override_guidance":"","check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone 'Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls' must be 'Enabled' and 'Disable' selected in the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3  Criteria: If the value \"270C\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000207","id":"V-223037"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59863","V-46997"],"group_id":"V-223037","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_title":"SRG-APP-000207","documentable":"false"},{"discussion":"This policy setting determines whether Internet Explorer runs Anti-Malware programs against ActiveX controls, to check if they're safe to load on pages.      If you enable this policy setting, Internet Explorer won't check with your Anti-Malware program to see if it's safe to create an instance of the ActiveX control. If you disable this policy setting, Internet Explorer always checks with your Anti-Malware program to see if it's safe to create an instance of the ActiveX control. If you don't configure this policy setting, Internet Explorer always checks with your Anti-Malware program to see if it's safe to create an instance of the ActiveX control. Users can turn this behavior on or off, using Internet Explorer Security settings.","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59871","V-47005"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone 'Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls' must be 'Enabled' and 'Disable' selected in the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4  Criteria: If the value \"270C\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000207","id":"V-223038"},"stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223038","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000207","severity":"medium","rule_id":"SV-223038r961086","false_positives":"","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-001662"],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone 'Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls' to 'Enabled' and select 'Disable' in the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Anti-Malware programs against ActiveX controls must be run for the Restricted Sites zone.","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223038r961086_rule","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:56800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:56800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '270C'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:56800 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '270C'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_version":"DTBI1051-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:568"},"weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223038","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"D4555D50-6BF7-1014-A015-F51F98033E38","potential_impacts":""},{"rule_version":"DTBI1060-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:578"},"weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223039","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"D455671C-6BF7-1014-8E52-FA4CDCD727FC","potential_impacts":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"If the system is on the SIPRNet, this requirement is NA.\n\nSet the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Internet Explorer &gt;&gt; âPrevent bypassing SmartScreen Filter warningsâ to âEnabledâ.   ","rule_title":"Prevent bypassing SmartScreen Filter warnings must be enabled.","rule_id_src":"SV-223039r961194_rule","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\PhishingFilter\\PreventOverride is a REG_DWORD equal to 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:57800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\PhishingFilter\\PreventOverride is a REG_DWORD equal to 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:57800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\PhishingFilter\\PreventOverride is a REG_DWORD equal to 1\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\PhishingFilter'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'PreventOverride'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:57800 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\PhishingFilter\\PreventOverride is a REG_DWORD equal to 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\PhishingFilter'\n                        : name equals 'PreventOverride'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","severity":"medium","rule_id":"SV-223039r961194","false_positives":"","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-001242"],"comments":null,"discussion":"This policy setting determines whether the user can bypass warnings from SmartScreen Filter. SmartScreen Filter prevents the user from browsing to or downloading from sites that are known to host malicious content. SmartScreen Filter also prevents the execution of files that are known to be malicious. If you enable this policy setting, SmartScreen Filter warnings block the user. If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, the user can bypass SmartScreen Filter warnings.","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":["SV-79201","V-64711"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-223039","title":"SRG-APP-000278"},"check_content":"If the system is on the SIPRNet, this requirement is NA.\n\nThe policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Internet Explorer &gt;&gt; âPrevent bypassing SmartScreen Filter warningsâ must be âEnabledâ. \n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\PhishingFilter. \n\nCriteria: If the value \"PreventOverride\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.\n","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223039","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278"},{"ccis":["CCI-001169"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223040r961089","severity":"medium","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000209","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223040","legacy_ids":["SV-79203","V-64713"],"check_content":"If the system is on the SIPRNet, this requirement is NA.\n\nThe policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Internet Explorer &gt;&gt; âPrevent bypassing SmartScreen Filter warnings about files that are not commonly downloaded from the internetâ must be âEnabledâ. \n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\PhishingFilter.\n\nCriteria: If the value \"PreventOverrideAppRepUnknown\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.\n","group_tree":{"id":"V-223040","title":"SRG-APP-000209"},"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"This policy setting determines whether the user can bypass warnings from SmartScreen Filter. SmartScreen Filter warns the user about executable files that Internet Explorer users do not commonly download from the internet. If you enable this policy setting, SmartScreen Filter warnings block the user. If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, the user can bypass SmartScreen Filter warnings.","uuid":"D45570A9-6BF7-1014-AFD2-AD7FBE952B6A","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223040","weight":"10.0","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:572"},"rule_version":"DTBI1065-IE11","ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\PhishingFilter\\PreventOverrideAppRepUnknown is a REG_DWORD equal to 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:57200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\PhishingFilter\\PreventOverrideAppRepUnknown is a REG_DWORD equal to 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:57200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\PhishingFilter\\PreventOverrideAppRepUnknown is a REG_DWORD equal to 1\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\PhishingFilter'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'PreventOverrideAppRepUnknown'\n\nStat