l.disa.fso.ie:tst:57400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Security\\ActiveX\\BlockNonAdminActiveXInstall is a REG_DWORD equal to 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:57400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Security\\ActiveX\\BlockNonAdminActiveXInstall is a REG_DWORD equal to 1\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Security\\ActiveX'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'BlockNonAdminActiveXInstall'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:57400 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Security\\ActiveX\\BlockNonAdminActiveXInstall is a REG_DWORD equal to 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Security\\ActiveX'\n                        : name equals 'BlockNonAdminActiveXInstall'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223041r961092_rule","rule_title":"Prevent per-user installation of ActiveX controls must be enabled.","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Internet Explorer &gt;&gt; âPrevent per-user installation of ActiveX controlsâ to âEnabledâ.   ","classification":"Unclassified","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D45579AB-6BF7-1014-931A-9373945D2929","group_id_src":"V-223041","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:574"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI1070-IE11","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","group_id":"V-223041","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_tree":{"id":"V-223041","title":"SRG-APP-000210"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Internet Explorer &gt;&gt; âPrevent per-user installation of ActiveX controlsâ must be âEnabledâ. \n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Security\\ActiveX. \n\nCriteria: If the value \"BlockNonAdminActiveXInstall\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.\n","legacy_ids":["SV-79205","V-64715"],"discussion":"This policy setting allows you to prevent the installation of ActiveX controls on a per-user basis. If you enable this policy setting, ActiveX controls cannot be installed on a per-user basis. If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, ActiveX controls can be installed on a per-user basis.","security_override_guidance":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001170"],"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223041r961092","severity":"medium"},{"group_id":"V-223042","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000427","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"This policy setting prevents the user from ignoring Secure Sockets Layer/Transport Layer Security (SSL/TLS) certificate errors that interrupt browsing (such as âexpiredâ, ârevokedâ, or âname mismatchâ errors) in Internet Explorer. If you enable this policy setting, the user cannot continue browsing. If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, the user can choose to ignore certificate errors and continue browsing.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000427","id":"V-223042"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Internet Explorer &gt;&gt; Internet Control Panel &gt;&gt; âPrevent ignoring certificate errorsâ must be âEnabledâ. \n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings. \n\nCriteria: If the value \"PreventIgnoreCertErrors\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.\n","legacy_ids":["SV-79207","V-64717"],"responsibility":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001954"],"severity":"medium","rule_id":"SV-223042r961596","false_positives":"","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223042r961596_rule","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\PreventIgnoreCertErrors is a REG_DWORD equal to 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:57500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\PreventIgnoreCertErrors is a REG_DWORD equal to 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:57500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\PreventIgnoreCertErrors is a REG_DWORD equal to 1\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'PreventIgnoreCertErrors'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:57500 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\PreventIgnoreCertErrors is a REG_DWORD equal to 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings'\n                        : name equals 'PreventIgnoreCertErrors'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","classification":"Unclassified","rule_title":"Prevent ignoring certificate errors option must be enabled.","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Internet Explorer &gt;&gt; Internet Control Panel &gt;&gt; âPrevent ignoring certificate errorsâ to âEnabledâ.   ","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223042","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D455879B-6BF7-1014-AC9C-FB1B1FC19288","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI1075-IE11","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:575","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"}},{"reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Internet Explorer &gt;&gt; Internet Control Panel &gt;&gt; Security Page &gt;&gt; Internet Zone &gt;&gt; âTurn on SmartScreen Filter scanâ to âEnabledâ, and select âEnableâ from the drop-down box.   ","rule_title":"Turn on SmartScreen Filter scan option for the Internet Zone must be enabled.","classification":"Unclassified","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3\\2301 is a REG_DWORD equal to 0)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:57700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3\\2301 is a REG_DWORD equal to 0\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:57700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3\\2301 is a REG_DWORD equal to 0\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\