\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3. \n\nCriteria: If the value \"2301\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.\n","discussion":"This policy setting controls whether SmartScreen Filter scans pages in this zone for malicious content. If you enable this policy setting, SmartScreen Filter scans pages in this zone for malicious content. If you disable this policy setting, SmartScreen Filter does not scan pages in this zone for malicious content. If you do not configure this policy setting, the user can choose whether SmartScreen Filter scans pages in this zone for malicious content.","security_override_guidance":"","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223043","rule_id":"SV-223043r961194","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-001242"],"comments":null,"responsibility":""},{"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"This policy setting controls whether SmartScreen Filter scans pages in this zone for malicious content. If you enable this policy setting, SmartScreen Filter scans pages in this zone for malicious content. If you disable this policy setting, SmartScreen Filter does not scan pages in this zone for malicious content. If you do not configure this policy setting, the user can choose whether SmartScreen Filter scans pages in this zone for malicious content.","group_tree":{"id":"V-223044","title":"SRG-APP-000278"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Internet Explorer &gt;&gt; Internet Control Panel &gt;&gt; Security Page &gt;&gt; Restricted Sites Zone &gt;&gt; âTurn on SmartScreen Filter scanâ must be âEnabledâ and âEnableâ selected from the drop-down box. \n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4. \n\nCriteria: If the value \"2301\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.\n","legacy_ids":["SV-79211","V-64721"],"group_id":"V-223044","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223044r961194","responsibility":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001242"],"classification":"Unclassified","rule_title":"Turn on SmartScreen Filter scan option for the Restricted Sites Zone must be enabled.","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Internet Explorer &gt;&gt; Internet Control Panel &gt;&gt; Security Page &gt;&gt; Restricted Sites Zone &gt;&gt; âTurn on SmartScreen Filter scanâ to âEnabledâ, and select âEnableâ from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_id_src":"SV-223044r961194_rule","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4\\2301 is a REG_DWORD equal to 0)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:57600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4\\2301 is a REG_DWORD equal to 0\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:57600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4\\2301 is a REG_DWORD equal to 0\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'H