\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:58701 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'CurrentBuildNumber'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:59000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Sz type and value is greater than or equal to 15063\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '15063'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\n                        : name equals 'CurrentBuildNumber'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994250000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '20348'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223055r961089_rule","rule_title":"VBScript must not be allowed to run in Internet Explorer (Restricted Sites zone).","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Internet Explorer &gt;&gt; Internet Control Panel &gt;&gt; Security Page &gt;&gt; Restricted Sites Zone &gt;&gt; \"Allow VBScript to run in Internet Explorer\" to \"Enabled\" and select \"Disable\" from the drop-down box.","reference_identifier":"4095","classification":"Unclassified","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D455FB42-6BF7-1014-ACF8-E445B220FD91","group_id_src":"V-223055","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:589"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI1130-IE11"},{"uuid":"D45604BC-6BF7-1014-9751-B3B2952F03E6","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-223056","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:591"},"rule_version":"DTBI1135-IE11","ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Developer Tools are disabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:59100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Developer Tools are disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:59100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Developer Tools registry\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\IEDevTools'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Disabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:59100 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword equals 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\IEDevTools'\n                        : name equals 'Disabled'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223056r961167_rule","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Internet Explorer &gt;&gt; Toolbars &gt;&gt; âTurn off Developer Toolsâ to âEnabledâ.","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Internet Explorer Development Tools Must Be Disabled.","classification":"Unclassified","ccis":["CCI-001312"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223056r961167","severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-APP-000266","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223056","legacy_ids":["SV-106631","V-97527"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Internet Explorer &gt;&gt; Toolbars &gt;&gt; âTurn off Developer Toolsâ must be âEnabledâ. \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKEY_LOCAL_Machine\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\IEDevTools\nCriteria: If the value \"Disabled\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000266","id":"V-223056"},"discussion":"While the risk associated with browser development tools is more related to the proper design of a web application, a risk vector remains within the browser. The developer tools allow end users and application developers to view and edit all types of web application related data via the browser. Page elements, source code, javascript, API calls, application data, etc. may all be viewed and potentially manipulated. Manipulation could be useful for troubleshooting legitimate issues, and this may be performed in a development environment. Manipulation could also be malicious and must be addressed.","security_override_guidance":""},{"third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Initialize and script ActiveX controls not marked as safe)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:43800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Initialize and script ActiveX controls not marked as safe\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:43800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Initialize and script ActiveX controls not marked as safe\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1201'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:43800 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Initialize and script ActiveX controls not marked as safe\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1201'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223057r961092_rule","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Initialize and script ActiveX controls not marked as safe' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"The Initialize and script ActiveX controls not marked as safe property must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"D4560E07-6BF7-1014-BAD8-9E0D7FCCBDC5","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223057","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:438"},"rule_version":"DTBI114-IE11","ia_controls":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223057","legacy_ids":["SV-59441","V-46577"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000210","id":"V-223057"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Initialize and script ActiveX controls not marked as safe' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1201\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"ActiveX controls not marked safe for scripting should not be executed. Although this is not a complete security measure for a control to be marked safe for scripting, if a control is not marked safe, it should not be initialized and executed.","ccis":["CCI-001170"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","rule_id":"SV-223057r961092","false_positives":"","severity":"medium"},{"mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223058r961863_rule","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Run ActiveX controls and plugins)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:43900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Run ActiveX controls and plugins\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:43900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Run ActiveX controls and plugins\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1200'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:43900 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Run ActiveX controls and plugins\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1200'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Run ActiveX controls and plugins' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","rule_title":"ActiveX controls and plug-ins must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","status":"not_a_finding","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223058","uuid":"D456172A-6BF7-1014-A0F9-F2C01943D281","potential_impacts":"","rule_version":"DTBI115-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:439","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223058","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"This policy setting allows you to manage whether ActiveX controls and plug-ins can be run on pages from the specified zone. ActiveX controls not marked as safe should not be executed. If you enable this policy setting, controls and plug-ins can run without user intervention. If you disable this policy setting, controls and plug-ins are prevented from running.","legacy_ids":["SV-59443","V-46579"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Run ActiveX controls and plugins' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1200\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"id":"V-223058","title":"SRG-APP-000516"},"responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"comments":null,"severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223058r961863"},{"discussion":"This policy setting allows management of whether ActiveX controls marked safe for scripting can interact with a script. If you enable this policy setting, script interaction can occur automatically without user intervention. ActiveX controls not marked as safe for scripting should not be executed. Although this is not a complete security measure for a control to be marked safe for scripting, if a control is not marked safe, it should not be initialized and executed.","security_override_guidance":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-223059","title":"SRG-APP-000210"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Script ActiveX controls marked safe for scripting' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1405\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59445","V-46581"],"group_id":"V-223059","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223059r961092","responsibility":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001170"],"classification":"Unclassified","rule_title":"ActiveX controls marked safe for scripting must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Script ActiveX controls marked safe for scripting' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223059r961092_rule","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Script ActiveX controls marked safe for scripting)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:44000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Script ActiveX controls marked safe for scripting\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:44000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Script ActiveX controls marked safe for scripting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1405'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:44000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Script ActiveX controls marked safe for scripting\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1405'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI116-IE11","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:440","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"group_id_src":"V-223059","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4561F8E-6BF7-1014-9325-E53CD617D246"},{"responsibility":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223060r960963","group_id":"V-223060","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Sites located in the Restricted Sites Zone are more likely to contain malicious payloads and therefore downloads from this zone should be blocked. Files should not be able to be downloaded from sites that are considered restricted. This policy setting allows you to manage whether file downloads are permitted from the zone. This option is determined by the zone of the page with the link causing the download, not the zone from which the file is delivered.","check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow file downloads' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1803\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"id":"V-223060","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59447","V-46583"],"status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223060","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4562770-6BF7-1014-8AE8-D83D3F3CBCC6","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI119-IE11","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:441","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-223060r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow file downloads)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:44100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow file downloads\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:44100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow file downloads\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1803'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:44100 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow file downloads\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1803'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","classification":"Unclassified","rule_title":"File downloads must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow file downloads' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   "},{"mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223061r960963_rule","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Java permissions)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:45300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Java permissions\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:45300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Java permissions\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1C00'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:45300 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Java permissions\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1C00'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","classification":"Unclassified","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable Java' from the drop-down box.  ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Java permissions must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223061","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","uuid":"D4562FCA-6BF7-1014-84FE-BC4EBA69122E","potential_impacts":"","rule_version":"DTBI121-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:453","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223061","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Java applications could contain malicious code; sites located in this security zone are more likely to be hosted by malicious individuals. This policy setting allows you to manage permissions for Java applets. If you enable this policy setting, options can be chosen from the drop-down box. Use of the Custom permission will control permissions settings individually. Use of the Low Safety permission enables applets to perform all operations. Use of the Medium Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox (an area in memory outside of which the program cannot make calls), plus adds capabilities like scratch space (a safe and secure storage area on the client computer) and a user-controlled file I/O. Use of the High Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox. If you disable this policy setting, Java applets cannot run. If you do not configure this policy setting, the permission is set to High Safety.","legacy_ids":["SV-59451","V-46587"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable Java' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1C00\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"id":"V-223061","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"comments":null,"severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223061r960963"},{"third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Access data sources across domains)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:44300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Access data sources across domains\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:44300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Access data sources across domains\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1406'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:44300 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Access data sources across domains\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1406'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_id_src":"SV-223062r1117169_rule","mitigation_control":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Access data sources across domains' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Accessing data sources across domains must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"D45639FE-6BF7-1014-8E0B-EA1CCB355A2C","potential_impacts":"","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223062","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:443","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI122-IE11","ia_controls":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000039","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223062","legacy_ids":["SV-59453","V-46589"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Access data sources across domains' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1406\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000039","id":"V-223062"},"discussion":"The ability to access data zones across domains could cause the user to unknowingly access content hosted on an unauthorized server. This policy setting allows you to manage whether Internet Explorer can access data from another security zone using the Microsoft XML Parser (MSXML) or ActiveX Data Objects (ADO).","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-001414"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223062r1117169","severity":"medium"},{"uuid":"D456412B-6BF7-1014-BAA6-A3090B1DAE63","potential_impacts":"","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223063","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:444","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI123-IE11","ia_controls":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow META REFRESH)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:44400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow META REFRESH\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:44400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow META REFRESH\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1608'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:44400 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow META REFRESH\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1608'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223063r961863_rule","mitigation_control":"","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow META REFRESH' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.","rule_title":"The Allow META REFRESH property must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","classification":"Unclassified","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223063r961863","severity":"medium","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223063","legacy_ids":["SV-59455","V-46591"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow META REFRESH' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1608\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516","id":"V-223063"},"discussion":"It is possible that users will unknowingly be redirected to a site hosting malicious content. 'Allow META REFRESH' must have a level of protection based upon the site being browsed. This policy setting allows you to manage whether a user's browser can be redirected to another web page if the author of the web page uses the Meta Refresh setting to redirect browsers to another web page.","security_override_guidance":""},{"status":"not_a_finding","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223064","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4564BDC-6BF7-1014-9482-F9BFFE137C5F","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI126-IE11","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:445","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-223064r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow drag and drop or copy and paste files)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:44500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow drag and drop or copy and paste files\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:44500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow drag and drop or copy and paste files\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1802'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:44500 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow drag and drop or copy and paste files\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1802'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","classification":"Unclassified","rule_title":"Functionality to drag and drop or copy and paste files must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow drag and drop or copy and paste files' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","responsibility":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"severity":"medium","rule_id":"SV-223064r960963","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-223064","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Content hosted on sites located in the Restricted Sites zone are more likely to contain malicious payloads and therefore this feature should be blocked for this zone. Drag and drop or copy and paste files must have a level of protection based upon the site being accessed.","check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow drag and drop or copy and paste files' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1802\" is REG_DWORD=3, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"id":"V-223064","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59457","V-46593"]},{"group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223065","legacy_ids":["SV-59461","V-46597"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223065"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Launching applications and files in an IFRAME' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1804\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","discussion":"This policy setting allows you to manage whether applications may be run and files may be downloaded from an IFRAME reference in the HTML of the pages in this zone. Launching of programs in IFRAME must have a level of protection based upon the site being accessed. If you enable this policy setting, applications can run and files can be downloaded from IFRAMEs on the pages in this zone without user intervention. If you disable this setting, users are prevented from running applications and downloading files from IFRAMEs on the pages in this zone.","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223065r960963","severity":"medium","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Launching applications and files in an IFRAME)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:44700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Launching applications and files in an IFRAME\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:44700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Launching applications and files in an IFRAME\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1804'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:44700 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Launching applications and files in an IFRAME\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1804'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223065r960963_rule","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Launching applications and files in an IFRAME' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","rule_title":"Launching programs and files in IFRAME must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"D45653F7-6BF7-1014-8317-C0FD827AFAD3","potential_impacts":"","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223065","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:447"},"rule_version":"DTBI128-IE11","ia_controls":""},{"false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223066r1117169","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-001414"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59463","V-46599"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000039","id":"V-223066"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Navigate windows and frames across different domains' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1607\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Frames navigating across different domains are a security concern, because the user may think they are accessing pages on one site while they are actually accessing pages on another site. It is possible that a website hosting malicious content could use this feature in a manner similar to cross-site scripting (XSS). This policy setting allows you to manage the opening of sub-frames and access of applications across different domains.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000039","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223066","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:448"},"rule_version":"DTBI129-IE11","ia_controls":"","uuid":"D4565B81-6BF7-1014-B14D-EBF2C0C0459D","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223066","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Navigate windows and frames across different domains' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box. ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Navigating windows and frames across different domains must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","classification":"Unclassified","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Navigate windows and frames across different domains)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:44800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Navigate windows and frames across different domains\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:44800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Navigate windows and frames across different domains\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1607'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:44800 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Navigate windows and frames across different domains\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1607'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223066r1117169_rule"},{"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Userdata persistence must have a level of protection based upon the site being accessed. This policy setting allows you to manage the preservation of information in the browser's history, in Favorites, in an XML store, or directly within a web page saved to disk. When a user returns to a persisted page, the state of the page can be restored if this policy setting is not appropriately configured.","legacy_ids":["SV-59465","V-46601"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Userdata persistence' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1606\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000231","id":"V-223067"},"stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223067","group_title":"SRG-APP-000231","documentable":"false","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223067r961128","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-001199"],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Userdata persistence' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Userdata persistence must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","rule_id_src":"SV-223067r961128_rule","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Userdata persistence)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:44900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Userdata persistence\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:44900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Userdata persistence\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1606'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:44900 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Userdata persistence\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1606'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_version":"DTBI132-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:449","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223067","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","uuid":"D4566309-6BF7-1014-AD7C-B51F9427C3BE","potential_impacts":""},{"rule_version":"DTBI133-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:450"},"weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223068","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"D4567436-6BF7-1014-8670-8FEC9BFC2659","potential_impacts":"","classification":"Unclassified","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow active scripting' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box. ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Active scripting must be disallowed (Restricted Sites Zone).","rule_id_src":"SV-223068r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow active scripting)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:45000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow active scripting\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:45000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow active scripting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1400'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:45000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow active scripting\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1400'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223068r960963","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"comments":null,"discussion":"Active scripts hosted on sites located in this zone are more likely to contain malicious code. Active scripting must have a level of protection based upon the site being accessed. This policy setting allows you to manage whether script code on pages in the zone are run.","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59467","V-46603"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow active scripting' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1400\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223068"},"stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223068","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141"},{"weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223069","status":"not_a_finding","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4567F70-6BF7-1014-AD41-8F5D238AD97B","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI134-IE11","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:451"},"rule_id_src":"SV-223069r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow cut, copy, or paste operations from the clipboard via script)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:45100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow cut, copy, or paste operations from the clipboard via script\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:45100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow cut, copy, or paste operations from the clipboard via script\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1407'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:45100 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow cut, copy, or paste operations from the clipboard via script\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1407'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","classification":"Unclassified","rule_title":"Clipboard operations via script must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow cut, copy or paste operations from the clipboard via script' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box. ","responsibility":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"severity":"medium","rule_id":"SV-223069r960963","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-223069","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","discussion":"A malicious script could use the clipboard in an undesirable manner, for example, if the user had recently copied confidential information to the clipboard while editing a document, a malicious script could harvest that information. It might be possible to exploit other vulnerabilities in order to send the harvested data to the attacker. Allow paste operations via script must have a level of protection based upon the site being accessed.","security_override_guidance":"","check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow cut, copy or paste operations from the clipboard via script' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1407\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223069"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59469","V-46605"]},{"documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000219","group_id":"V-223070","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_tree":{"id":"V-223070","title":"SRG-APP-000219"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Logon options' must be 'Enabled', and 'Anonymous logon' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1A00\" is REG_DWORD = 196608 (decimal), this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59471","V-46607"],"discussion":"Users could submit credentials to servers operated by malicious individuals who could then attempt to connect to legitimate servers with those captured credentials. Care must be taken with user credentials, automatic logon performance, and how default Windows credentials are passed to the websites. This policy setting allows management of settings for logon options. If you enable this policy setting, you can choose from varying logon options. âAnonymous logonâ disables HTTP authentication and uses the guest account only for the Common Internet File System (CIFS) protocol. âPrompt for user name and passwordâ queries users for user IDs and passwords. After a user is queried, these values can be used silently for the remainder of the session. âAutomatic logon only in Intranet zoneâ queries users for user IDs and passwords in other zones. After a user is queried, these values can be used silently for the remainder of the session. âAutomatic logon with current user name and passwordâ attempts logon using Windows NT Challenge Response. If Windows NT Challenge Response is supported by the server, the logon uses the user's network user name and password for login. If Windows NT Challenge Response is not supported by the server, the user is queried to provide the user name and password. If you disable this policy setting, logon is set to âAutomatic logon only in Intranet zoneâ. If you do not configure this policy setting, logon is set to âAutomatic logon only in Intranet zoneâ. The most secure option is to configure this setting to âEnabledâ; âAnonymous logonâ. This will prevent users from submitting credentials to servers in this security zone.","security_override_guidance":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001184"],"responsibility":"","rule_id":"SV-223070r1043178","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Logon options)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:45200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Logon options\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:45200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Logon options\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1A00'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:45200 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Logon options\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '196608'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1A00'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '196608'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223070r1043178_rule","rule_title":"Logon options must be configured and enforced (Restricted Sites zone).","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Logon options' to 'Enabled', and select 'Anonymous logon' from the drop-down box.","classification":"Unclassified","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4568AFA-6BF7-1014-9533-B9425453767C","group_id_src":"V-223070","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:452","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI136-IE11"},{"rule_id":"SV-223071r960879","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000169"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59473","V-46609"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-223071","title":"SRG-APP-000089"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Delete Browsing History -&gt; 'Disable Configuring History' must be 'Enabled', and '40' entered in 'Days to keep pages in History'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Control Panel Criteria: If the value \"History\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding. AND  Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Url History Criteria: If the value \"DaysToKeep\" is REG_DWORD = 40 (decimal), this is not a finding.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"This setting specifies the number of days that Internet Explorer keeps track of the pages viewed in the History List. The delete Browsing History option can be accessed using Tools, Internet Options, \"General\" tab, and then click Settings under Browsing History. If you enable this policy setting, a user cannot set the number of days that Internet Explorer keeps track of the pages viewed in the History List. The number of days that Internet Explorer keeps track of the pages viewed in the History List must be specified. Users will not be able to delete browsing history. If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, a user can set the number of days that Internet Explorer tracks views of pages in the History List. Users can delete browsing history.","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000089","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223071","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:513"},"rule_version":"DTBI300-IE11","ia_controls":"","uuid":"D4569473-6BF7-1014-B3D8-DC0CBEC763B5","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223071","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Delete Browsing History -&gt; 'Disable Configuring History' to 'Enabled', and enter '40' in 'Days to keep pages in History'.","rule_title":"Configuring History setting must be set to 40 days.","classification":"Unclassified","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Delete Browsing History\\Disable Configuring History must be Enabled)\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Delete Browsing History\\40 entered in Days to keep pages in History)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:51301 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Delete Browsing History\\Disable Configuring History must be Enabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:51301 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Delete Browsing History\\Disable Configuring History must be Enabled\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Control Panel'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'History'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:51301 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Delete Browsing History\\Disable Configuring History must be Enabled\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Control Panel'\n                        : name equals 'History'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:51300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Delete Browsing History\\40 entered in Days to keep pages in History\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:51300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Delete Browsing History\\40 entered in Days to keep pages in History\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Url History'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DaysToKeep'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:51300 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Delete Browsing History\\40 entered in Days to keep pages in History\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '40'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Url History'\n                        : name equals 'DaysToKeep'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '40'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223071r960879_rule","mitigation_control":""},{"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:419","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI318-IE11","ia_controls":"","uuid":"D4569D12-6BF7-1014-916B-FBD71FC48072","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-223072","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer 'Security Zones: Do not allow users to add/delete sites' to 'Enabled'.","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Internet Explorer must be set to disallow users to add/delete sites.","classification":"Unclassified","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Security Zones: Do Not Allow Users to Add/Delete Sites)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:41900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Security Zones: Do Not Allow Users to Add/Delete Sites\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:41900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Security Zones: Do Not Allow Users to Add/Delete Sites\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Security_zones_map_edit'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:41900 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Security Zones: Do Not Allow Users to Add/Delete Sites\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings'\n                        : name equals 'Security_zones_map_edit'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223072r960963_rule","rule_id":"SV-223072r960963","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59479","V-46615"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223072"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer 'Security Zones: Do not allow users to add/delete sites' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings Criteria: If the value \"Security_zones_map_edit\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.","discussion":"This setting prevents users from adding sites to various security zones. Users should not be able to add sites to different zones, as this could allow them to bypass security controls of the system. If you do not configure this policy setting, users will be able to add or remove sites from the Trusted Sites and Restricted Sites zones at will and change settings in the Local Intranet zone. This configuration could allow sites that host malicious mobile code to be added to these zones, and users could execute the code.","security_override_guidance":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223072"},{"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:418","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI319-IE11","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D456A545-6BF7-1014-9560-CAEFAB48E6A9","group_id_src":"V-223073","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","rule_title":"Internet Explorer must be configured to disallow users to change policies.","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer 'Security Zones: Do not allow users to change policies' to 'Enabled'.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","classification":"Unclassified","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Security Zones: Do Not Allow Users to Change Policies)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:41800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Security Zones: Do Not Allow Users to Change Policies\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:41800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Security Zones: Do Not Allow Users to Change Policies\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Security_options_edit'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:41800 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Security Zones: Do Not Allow Users to Change Policies\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings'\n                        : name equals 'Security_options_edit'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223073r961863_rule","rule_id":"SV-223073r961863","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-223073","title":"SRG-APP-000516"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer 'Security Zones: Do not allow users to change policies' must be 'Enabled'.  Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings Criteria: If the value \"Security_options_edit\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59481","V-46617"],"discussion":"Users who change their Internet Explorer security settings could enable the execution of dangerous types of code from the Internet and websites listed in the Restricted Sites zone in the browser. This setting prevents users from changing the Internet Explorer policies on the machine. Policy changes should be made by administrators only, so this setting should be enabled. If you enable this policy setting, you disable the \"Custom level\" button and \"Security\" level for this zone slider on the Security tab in the Internet Options dialog box. If this policy setting is disabled or not configured, users will be able to change the settings for security zones. It prevents users from changing security zone policy settings that are established by the administrator.","security_override_guidance":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516","documentable":"false","group_id":"V-223073","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D"},{"false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223074r961863","severity":"medium","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"responsibility":"","check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer 'Security Zones: Use only machine settings' must be 'Enabled'.  Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings Criteria: If the value \"Security_HKLM_only\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"id":"V-223074","title":"SRG-APP-000516"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59483","V-46619"],"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Users who change their Internet Explorer security settings could enable the execution of dangerous types of code from the Internet and websites listed in the Restricted Sites zone in the browser. This setting enforces consistent security zone settings to all users of the computer. Security zones control browser behavior at various websites and it is desirable to maintain a consistent policy for all users of a machine. This policy setting affects how security zone changes apply to different users. If you enable this policy setting, changes that one user makes to a security zone will apply to all users of that computer. If this policy setting is disabled or not configured, users of the same computer are allowed to establish their own security zone settings.","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516","group_id":"V-223074","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:417","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI320-IE11","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D456AE10-6BF7-1014-97E7-AD319A169475","status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223074","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_title":"Internet Explorer must be configured to use machine settings.","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer 'Security Zones: Use only machine settings' to 'Enabled'. ","classification":"Unclassified","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Security Zones: Use Only Machine Settings)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:41700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Security Zones: Use Only Machine Settings\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:41700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Security Zones: Use Only Machine Settings\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Security_HKLM_only'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:41700 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Security Zones: Use Only Machine Settings\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings'\n                        : name equals 'Security_HKLM_only'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223074r961863_rule"},{"weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223075","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"D456B690-6BF7-1014-B7D3-9E84D3BCED63","potential_impacts":"","rule_version":"DTBI325-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:457","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223075r961863_rule","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Turn off the Security Settings Check feature)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:45700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Turn off the Security Settings Check feature\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:45700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Turn off the Security Settings Check feature\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Security'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableSecuritySettingsCheck'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:45700 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Turn off the Security Settings Check feature\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Security'\n                        : name equals 'DisableSecuritySettingsCheck'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; 'Turn off the Security Settings Check feature' to 'Disabled'.   ","rule_title":"Security checking features must be enforced.","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"comments":null,"severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223075r961863","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223075","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516","documentable":"false","discussion":"This policy setting turns off the Security Settings Check feature, which checks Internet Explorer security settings to determine when the settings put Internet Explorer at risk. If you enable this policy setting, the security settings check will not be performed. If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, the security settings check will be performed.","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59485","V-46621"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; 'Turn off the Security Settings Check feature' must be 'Disabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Security Criteria: If the value \"DisableSecuritySettingsCheck\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"id":"V-223075","title":"SRG-APP-000516"}},{"documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223076","legacy_ids":["SV-59489","V-46625"],"check_content":"Note: Some legitimate software and controls may have an invalid signature. You should carefully test such software in isolation before it is allowed to be used on an organization's network.\n\nThe policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Advanced Page -&gt; 'Allow software to run or install even if the signature is invalid' must be 'Disabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Download Criteria: If the value \"RunInvalidSignatures\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"id":"V-223076","title":"SRG-APP-000210"},"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Microsoft ActiveX controls and file downloads often have digital signatures attached that certify the file's integrity and the identity of the signer (creator) of the software. Such signatures help ensure unmodified software is downloaded and the user can positively identify the signer to determine whether you trust them enough to run their software.","ccis":["CCI-001170"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223076r961092","severity":"medium","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page \\Allow Software to Run or Install Even if the Signature is Invalid)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:45900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page \\Allow Software to Run or Install Even if the Signature is Invalid\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:45900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page \\Allow Software to Run or Install Even if the Signature is Invalid\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Download'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'RunInvalidSignatures'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:45900 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page \\Allow Software to Run or Install Even if the Signature is Invalid\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Download'\n                        : name equals 'RunInvalidSignatures'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_id_src":"SV-223076r961092_rule","mitigation_control":"","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Advanced Page -&gt; 'Allow software to run or install even if the signature is invalid' to 'Disabled'. ","rule_title":"Software must be disallowed to run or install with invalid signatures.","classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"D456BF0E-6BF7-1014-A97B-A7DED16F4EAB","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223076","mitigations":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:459","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI350-IE11","ia_controls":""},{"mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223077r961131_rule","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page Turn on 64-bit tab processes when running in Enhanced Protected Mode on 64-bit versions of Windows)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:56400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page Turn on 64-bit tab processes when running in Enhanced Protected Mode on 64-bit versions of Windows\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:56400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page Turn on 64-bit tab processes when running in Enhanced Protected Mode on 64-bit versions of Windows\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Isolation64Bit'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:56400 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page Turn on 64-bit tab processes when running in Enhanced Protected Mode on 64-bit versions of Windows\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main'\n                        : name equals 'Isolation64Bit'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","classification":"Unclassified","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Advanced Page 'Turn on 64-bit tab processes when running in Enhanced Protected Mode on 64-bit versions of Windows' to 'Enabled'.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"The 64-bit tab processes, when running in Enhanced Protected Mode on 64-bit versions of Windows, must be turned on.","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223077","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"D456C7B0-6BF7-1014-886D-ED32C670F18D","potential_impacts":"","rule_version":"DTBI356-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:564","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223077","group_title":"SRG-APP-000233","documentable":"false","discussion":"This policy setting determines whether Internet Explorer 11 uses 64-bit processes (for greater security) or 32-bit processes (for greater compatibility) when running in Enhanced Protected Mode on 64-bit versions of Windows.Important: Some ActiveX controls and toolbars may not be available when 64-bit processes are used. If you enable this policy setting, Internet Explorer 11 will use 64-bit tab processes when running in Enhanced Protected Mode on 64-bit versions of Windows. If you disable this policy setting, Internet Explorer 11 will use 32-bit tab processes when running in Enhanced Protected Mode on 64-bit versions of Windows. If you don't configure this policy setting, users can turn this feature on or off using Internet Explorer settings. This feature is turned off by default.","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59861","V-46995"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000233","id":"V-223077"},"check_content":"Note: If McAfee ENS Web Control is being used, this is Not Applicable.\n\nThe policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Advanced Page 'Turn on 64-bit tab processes when running in Enhanced Protected Mode on 64-bit versions of Windows' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main Criteria: If the value \"Isolation64Bit\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-001084"],"comments":null,"severity":"medium","rule_id":"SV-223077r961131","false_positives":""},{"legacy_ids":["SV-59493","V-46629"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000175","id":"V-223078"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Advanced Page -&gt; 'Check for server certificate revocation' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings Criteria: If the value \"CertificateRevocation\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"This policy setting allows you to manage whether Internet Explorer will check revocation status of servers' certificates. Certificates are revoked when they have been compromised or are no longer valid, and this option protects users from submitting confidential data to a site that may be fraudulent or not secure. If you enable this policy setting, Internet Explorer will check to see if server certificates have been revoked. If you disable this policy setting, Internet Explorer will not check server certificates to see if they have been revoked. If you do not configure this policy setting, Internet Explorer will not check server certificates to see if they have been revoked.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-APP-000605","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000175","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223078","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223078r961038","severity":"low","ccis":["CCI-000185"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Advanced Page -&gt; 'Check for server certificate revocation' to 'Enabled'.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Checking for server certificate revocation must be enforced.","classification":"Unclassified","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page \\Check for Server Certificate Revocation)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:46100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page \\Check for Server Certificate Revocation\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:46100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page \\Check for Server Certificate Revocation\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'CertificateRevocation'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:46100 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page \\Check for Server Certificate Revocation\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings'\n                        : name equals 'CertificateRevocation'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223078r961038_rule","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:461"},"rule_version":"DTBI365-IE11","ia_controls":"","uuid":"D456D05B-6BF7-1014-9746-F17239432CD1","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223078","weight":"10.0","mitigations":""},{"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Advanced Page -&gt; 'Check for signatures on downloaded programs' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Download Criteria: If the value \"CheckExeSignatures\" is REG_SZ = yes, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000131","id":"V-223079"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59497","V-46633"],"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"This policy setting allows you to manage whether Internet Explorer checks for digital signatures (which identifies the publisher of signed software and verifies it has not been modified or tampered with) on user computers before downloading executable programs. If you enable this policy setting, Internet Explorer will check the digital signatures of executable programs and display their identities before downloading them to the user computers. If you disable this policy setting, Internet Explorer will not check the digital signatures of executable programs or display their identities before downloading them to the user computers. If you do not configure this policy, Internet Explorer will not check the digital signatures of executable programs or display their identities before downloading them to the user computers.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000131","documentable":"false","group_id":"V-223079","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","rule_id":"SV-223079r960954","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001749"],"responsibility":"","rule_title":"Checking for signatures on downloaded programs must be enforced.","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Advanced Page -&gt; 'Check for signatures on downloaded programs' to 'Enabled'.   ","classification":"Unclassified","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page \\Check for Signature on Downloaded Programs)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:46200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page \\Check for Signature on Downloaded Programs\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:46200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page \\Check for Signature on Downloaded Programs\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Download'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'CheckExeSignatures'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:46200 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Advanced Page \\Check for Signature on Downloaded Programs\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to 'yes'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Download'\n                        : name equals 'CheckExeSignatures'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'yes'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223079r960954_rule","mitigation_control":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:462"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI370-IE11","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D456DB2F-6BF7-1014-915F-A4E7831EA618","status":"not_a_finding","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223079"},{"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; 'Intranet Sites: Include all network paths (UNCs)' to 'Disabled'.   ","rule_title":"All network paths (UNCs) for Intranet sites must be disallowed.","rule_id_src":"SV-223080r961863_rule","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Intranet Sites: Include all network paths (UNCs))\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:46300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Intranet Sites: Include all network paths (UNCs)\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:46300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Intranet Sites: Include all network paths (UNCs)\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\ZoneMap'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'UNCAsIntranet'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:46300 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Intranet Sites: Include all network paths (UNCs)\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\ZoneMap'\n                        : name equals 'UNCAsIntranet'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","rule_version":"DTBI375-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:463"},"group_id_src":"V-223080","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"D456E439-6BF7-1014-B218-9808D87ABB46","potential_impacts":"","discussion":"Some UNC paths could refer to servers not managed by the organization, which means they could host malicious content; and therefore, it is safest to not include all UNC paths in the Intranet Sites zone. This policy setting controls whether URLs representing UNCs are mapped into the local Intranet security zone. If you enable this policy setting, all network paths are mapped into the Intranet Zone. If you disable this policy setting, network paths are not necessarily mapped into the Intranet Zone (other rules might map one there). If you do not configure this policy setting, users choose whether network paths are mapped into the Intranet Zone.","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59499","V-46635"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; 'Intranet Sites: Include all network paths (UNCs)' must be 'Disabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\ZoneMap Criteria: If the value \"UNCAsIntranet\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516","id":"V-223080"},"stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223080","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223080r961863","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"comments":null},{"group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","group_id":"V-223081","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Allow script-initiated windows without size or position constraints' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"2102\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223081"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59501","V-46637"],"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"This policy setting allows you to manage restrictions on script-initiated pop-up windows and windows including the title and status bars. If you enable this policy setting, Windows Restrictions security will not apply in this zone. The security zone runs without the added layer of security provided by this feature. If you disable this policy setting, the possible harmful actions contained in script-initiated pop-up windows and windows including the title and status bars cannot be run. This Internet Explorer security feature will be on in this zone as dictated by the Scripted Windows Security Restrictions feature control setting for the process. If you do not configure this policy setting, the possible harmful actions contained in script-initiated pop-up windows and windows including the title and status bars cannot be run. This Internet Explorer security feature will be on in this zone as dictated by the Scripted Windows Security Restrictions feature control setting for the process.","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223081r960963","severity":"medium","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow script-initiated windows without size or position constraints)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:46400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow script-initiated windows without size or position constraints\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:46400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow script-initiated windows without size or position constraints\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '2102'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:46400 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow script-initiated windows without size or position constraints\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '2102'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223081r960963_rule","rule_title":"Script-initiated windows without size or position constraints must be disallowed (Internet zone).","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Allow script-initiated windows without size or position constraints' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box. ","reference_identifier":"4095","classification":"Unclassified","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D456ED14-6BF7-1014-9A11-8B75091499D5","status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223081","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:464","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI385-IE11"},{"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI390-IE11","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:465","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223082","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D456F5CD-6BF7-1014-9E2B-82CC66A7E653","classification":"Unclassified","rule_title":"Script-initiated windows without size or position constraints must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow script-initiated windows without size or position constraints' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.  ","rule_id_src":"SV-223082r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow script-initiated windows without size or position constraints)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:46500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow script-initiated windows without size or position constraints\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:46500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow script-initiated windows without size or position constraints\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '2102'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:46500 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow script-initiated windows without size or position constraints\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '2102'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223082r960963","responsibility":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"discussion":"This policy setting allows you to manage restrictions on script-initiated pop-up windows and windows including the title and status bars. If you enable this policy setting, Windows Restrictions security will not apply in this zone. The security zone runs without the added layer of security provided by this feature. If you disable this policy setting, the possible harmful actions contained in script-initiated pop-up windows and windows including the title and status bars cannot be run. This Internet Explorer security feature will be on in this zone as dictated by the Scripted Windows Security Restrictions feature control setting for the process. If you do not configure this policy setting, the possible harmful actions contained in script-initiated pop-up windows and windows including the title and status bars cannot be run. This Internet Explorer security feature will be on in this zone as dictated by the Scripted Windows Security Restrictions feature control setting for the process.","security_override_guidance":"","check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow script-initiated windows without size or position constraints' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"2102\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223082"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59503","V-46639"],"group_id":"V-223082","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141"},{"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:466"},"rule_version":"DTBI395-IE11","ia_controls":"","uuid":"D456FDC2-6BF7-1014-8E7D-A83106C35764","potential_impacts":"","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223083","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Allow Scriptlets' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box. ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Scriptlets must be disallowed (Internet zone).","classification":"Unclassified","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow Scriptlets)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:46600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow Scriptlets\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:46600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow Scriptlets\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1209'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:46600 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Allow Scriptlets\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '1209'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_id_src":"SV-223083r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223083r960963","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59505","V-46641"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223083"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Allow Scriptlets' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"1209\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","discussion":"This policy setting allows you to manage whether scriptlets can be allowed. Scriptlets hosted on sites located in this zone are more likely to contain malicious code. If you enable this policy setting, users will be able to run scriptlets. If you disable this policy setting, users will not be able to run scriptlets. If you do not configure this policy setting, a scriptlet can be enabled or disabled by the user.","security_override_guidance":"","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223083"},{"discussion":"This policy setting determines whether users will be prompted for non user-initiated file downloads. Regardless of this setting, users will receive file download dialogs for user-initiated downloads. Users may accept downloads that they did not request, and those downloaded files may include malicious code. If you enable this setting, users will receive a file download dialog for automatic download attempts. If you disable or do not configure this setting, file downloads that are not user-initiated will be blocked, and users will see the information bar instead of the file download dialog. Users can then click the information bar to allow the file download prompt.","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59507","V-46643"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223084"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Automatic prompting for file downloads' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"2200\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223084","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223084r960963","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Automatic prompting for file downloads' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","rule_title":"Automatic prompting for file downloads must be disallowed (Internet zone).","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223084r960963_rule","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Automatic prompting for file downloads)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:46700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Automatic prompting for file downloads\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:46700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Automatic prompting for file downloads\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '2200'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:46700 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Automatic prompting for file downloads\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '2200'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_version":"DTBI415-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:467","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223084","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"D457071B-6BF7-1014-B58F-CC00172ECEA3","potential_impacts":""},{"potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4570F39-6BF7-1014-8E72-A2CF41EE314E","status":"not_a_finding","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223085","weight":"10.0","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:468"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI425-IE11","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Local Machine Zone\\Java permissions)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:46800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Local Machine Zone\\Java permissions\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:46800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Local Machine Zone\\Java permissions\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\0'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1C00'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:46800 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Local Machine Zone\\Java permissions\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\0'\n                        : name equals '1C00'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223085r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Java permissions must be disallowed (Local Machine zone).","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Local Machine Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable Java' from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223085r960963","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","group_id":"V-223085","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_tree":{"id":"V-223085","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Local Machine Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable Java' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following keys: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\0 Criteria: If the value \"1C00\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59509","V-46645"],"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Java applications could contain malicious code. This policy setting allows you to manage permissions for Java applets. If you enable this policy setting, options can be chosen from the drop-down box. Use of the Custom permission will control permissions settings individually. Use of the Low Safety permission enables applets to perform all operations. Use of the Medium Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox (an area in memory outside of which the program cannot make calls), plus adds capabilities like scratch space (a safe and secure storage area on the client computer) and a user-controlled file I/O. Use of the High Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox. If you disable this policy setting, Java applets cannot run. If you do not configure this policy setting, the permission is set to High Safety.  "},{"responsibility":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001662"],"severity":"medium","rule_id":"SV-223086r961086","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-223086","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000207","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"This policy setting determines whether Internet Explorer runs Anti-Malware programs against ActiveX controls, to check if they're safe to load on pages.      If you enable this policy setting, Internet Explorer won't check with your Anti-Malware program to see if it's safe to create an instance of the ActiveX control. If you disable this policy setting, Internet Explorer always checks with your Anti-Malware program to see if it's safe to create an instance of the ActiveX control. If you don't configure this policy setting, Internet Explorer won't check with your Anti-Malware program to see if it's safe to create an instance of the ActiveX control. Users can turn this behavior on or off, using Internet Explorer Security settings.","group_tree":{"id":"V-223086","title":"SRG-APP-000207"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt;Local Machine Zone 'Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls' must be 'Enabled' and 'Disable' selected in the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\0  Criteria: If the value \"270C\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59869","V-47003"],"status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223086","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4571765-6BF7-1014-B6F1-BA765ED06594","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI426-IE11","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:567","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-223086r961086_rule","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Local Machine Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:56700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Local Machine Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:56700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Local Machine Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\0'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '270C'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:56700 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Local Machine Zone Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\0'\n                        : name equals '270C'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","classification":"Unclassified","rule_title":"Anti-Malware programs against ActiveX controls must be run for the Local Machine zone.","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer-&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Local Machine Zone 'Don't run antimalware programs against ActiveX controls' to 'Enabled' and select 'Disable' in the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down Local Machine Zone\\Java permissions)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:46900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down Local Machine Zone\\Java permissions\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:46900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down Local Machine Zone\\Java permissions\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Lockdown_Zones\\0'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1C00'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:46900 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down Local Machine Zone\\Java permissions\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Lockdown_Zones\\0'\n                        : name equals '1C00'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223087r960963_rule","rule_title":"Java permissions must be disallowed (Locked Down Local Machine zone).","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Locked-Down Local Machine Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable Java' from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","classification":"Unclassified","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4571F98-6BF7-1014-8BB1-9F014549BB48","group_id_src":"V-223087","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:469"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI430-IE11","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","group_id":"V-223087","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Locked-Down Local Machine Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable Java' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following keys: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Lockdown_Zones\\0 Criteria: If the value \"1C00\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223087"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59511","V-46647"],"discussion":"Java applications could contain malicious code. This policy setting allows you to manage permissions for Java applets. If you enable this policy setting, options can be chosen from the drop-down box. Use of the Custom permission will control permissions settings individually. Use of the Low Safety permission enables applets to perform all operations. Use of the Medium Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox (an area in memory outside of which the program cannot make calls), plus adds capabilities like scratch space (a safe and secure storage area on the client computer) and a user-controlled file I/O. Use of the High Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox. If you disable this policy setting, Java applets cannot run. If you do not configure this policy setting, the permission is set to High Safety.","security_override_guidance":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223087r960963","severity":"medium"},{"rule_id_src":"SV-223088r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down Intranet Zone\\Java permissions)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:47000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down Intranet Zone\\Java permissions\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:47000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down Intranet Zone\\Java permissions\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Lockdown_Zones\\1'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1C00'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:47000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down Intranet Zone\\Java permissions\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Lockdown_Zones\\1'\n                        : name equals '1C00'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","classification":"Unclassified","rule_title":"Java permissions must be disallowed (Locked Down Intranet zone).","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Locked-Down Intranet Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable Java' from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223088","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4572A55-6BF7-1014-ABA8-A1500857513A","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI435-IE11","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:470"},"group_id":"V-223088","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Java applications could contain malicious code. This policy setting allows you to manage permissions for Java applets. If you enable this policy setting, options can be chosen from the drop-down box. Use of the Custom permission will control permissions settings individually. Use of the Low Safety permission enables applets to perform all operations. Use of the Medium Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox (an area in memory outside of which the program cannot make calls), plus adds capabilities like scratch space (a safe and secure storage area on the client computer) and a user-controlled file I/O. Use of the High Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox. If you disable this policy setting, Java applets cannot run. If you do not configure this policy setting, the permission is set to High Safety.","check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Locked-Down Intranet Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable Java' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following keys: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Lockdown_Zones\\1 Criteria: If the value\" 1C00\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"id":"V-223088","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59513","V-46649"],"responsibility":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"severity":"medium","rule_id":"SV-223088r960963","false_positives":""},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down Trusted Sites Zone\\Java permissions)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:47100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down Trusted Sites Zone\\Java permissions\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:47100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down Trusted Site Zone\\Java permissions\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Lockdown_Zones\\2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1C00'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:47100 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down Trusted Sites Zone\\Java permissions\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Lockdown_Zones\\2'\n                        : name equals '1C00'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223089r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Java permissions must be disallowed (Locked Down Trusted Sites zone).","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Locked-Down Trusted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable Java' from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","classification":"Unclassified","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4573350-6BF7-1014-964D-8C83E92BBBDF","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223089","mitigations":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:471","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI440-IE11","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","group_id":"V-223089","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Locked-Down Trusted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable Java' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following keys: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Lockdown_Zones\\2 Criteria: If the value \"1C00\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223089"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59517","V-46653"],"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Java applications could contain malicious code; sites located in this security zone are more likely to be hosted by malicious individuals. This policy setting allows you to manage permissions for Java applets. If you enable this policy setting, options can be chosen from the drop-down box. Use of the Custom permission will control permissions settings individually. Use of the Low Safety permission enables applets to perform all operations. Use of the Medium Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox (an area in memory outside of which the program cannot make calls), plus adds capabilities like scratch space (a safe and secure storage area on the client computer) and a user-controlled file I/O. Use of the High Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox. If you disable this policy setting, Java applets cannot run. If you do not configure this policy setting, the permission is set to High Safety. ","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223089r960963","severity":"medium"},{"rule_id":"SV-223090r960963","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59527","V-46663"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-223090","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Locked-Down Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable Java' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following keys: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Lockdown_Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1C00\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","discussion":"Java applications could contain malicious code. This policy setting allows you to manage permissions for Java applets. If you enable this policy setting, options can be chosen from the drop-down box. Use of the Custom permission will control permissions settings individually. Use of the Low Safety permission enables applets to perform all operations. Use of the Medium Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox (an area in memory outside of which the program cannot make calls), plus adds capabilities like scratch space (a safe and secure storage area on the client computer) and a user-controlled file I/O. Use of the High Safety permission enables applets to run in their sandbox. If you disable this policy setting, Java applets cannot run. If you do not configure this policy setting, the permission is set to High Safety. ","security_override_guidance":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223090","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:473","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI450-IE11","ia_controls":"","uuid":"D4573BA0-6BF7-1014-8733-DC0430E81519","potential_impacts":"","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223090","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Locked-Down Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Java permissions' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable Java' from the drop-down box.  ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Java permissions must be disallowed (Locked Down Restricted Sites zone).","classification":"Unclassified","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down restricted Sites Zone\\Java permissions)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:47300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down restricted Sites Zone\\Java permissions\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:47300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down Restricted Sites Zone\\Java permissions\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Lockdown_Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '1C00'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:47300 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Locked Down Restricted Sites Zone\\Java permissions\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Lockdown_Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1C00'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223090r960963_rule"},{"third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Loose or un-compiled XAML files)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:47400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Loose or un-compiled XAML files\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:47400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Loose or un-compiled XAML files\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '2402'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:47400 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Loose or un-compiled XAML files\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '2402'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_id_src":"SV-223091r961863_rule","mitigation_control":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Allow loading of XAML files' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"XAML files must be disallowed (Internet zone).","classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"D45743E9-6BF7-1014-B0B3-F475DCB2A8CB","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223091","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:474","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI455-IE11","ia_controls":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223091","legacy_ids":["SV-59529","V-46665"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-223091","title":"SRG-APP-000516"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Allow loading of XAML files' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"2402\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"These are eXtensible Application Markup Language (XAML) files. XAML is an XML-based declarative markup language commonly used for creating rich user interfaces and graphics that leverage the Windows Presentation Foundation. If you enable this policy setting and the drop-down box is set to Enable, XAML files will be automatically loaded inside Internet Explorer. Users will not be able to change this behavior. If the drop-down box is set to Prompt, users will receive a prompt for loading XAML files. If you disable this policy setting, XAML files will not be loaded inside Internet Explorer. Users will not be able to change this behavior. If you do not configure this policy setting, users will have the freedom to decide whether to load XAML files inside Internet Explorer.","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","rule_id":"SV-223091r961863","false_positives":"","severity":"medium"},{"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow loading of XAML files' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","rule_title":"XAML files must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223092r961863_rule","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Loose XAML files)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:47500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Loose XAML files\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:47500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Loose XAML files\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '2402'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:47500 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Loose or XAML files\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '2402'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_version":"DTBI460-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:475","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223092","mitigations":"","uuid":"D4574C8A-6BF7-1014-9386-88DF2B8AFB2C","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"These are eXtensible Application Markup Language (XAML) files. XAML is an XML-based declarative markup language commonly used for creating rich user interfaces and graphics that leverage the Windows Presentation Foundation. If you enable this policy setting and the drop-down box is set to Enable, XAML files will be automatically loaded inside Internet Explorer. Users will not be able to change this behavior. If the drop-down box is set to Prompt, users will receive a prompt for loading XAML files. If you disable this policy setting, XAML files will not be loaded inside Internet Explorer. Users will not be able to change this behavior. If you do not configure this policy setting, users will have the freedom to decide whether to load XAML files inside Internet Explorer.","legacy_ids":["SV-59533","V-46669"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516","id":"V-223092"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow loading of XAML files' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"2402\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223092","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516","documentable":"false","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223092r961863","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"comments":null},{"comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001084"],"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223093r961131","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000233","documentable":"false","group_id":"V-223093","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_tree":{"id":"V-223093","title":"SRG-APP-000233"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Turn on Protected Mode' must be 'Enabled', and 'Enable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"2500\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59545","V-46681"],"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Protected Mode protects Internet Explorer from exploited vulnerabilities by reducing the locations Internet Explorer can write to in the registry and the file system. If you enable this policy setting, Protected Mode will be turned on. Users will not be able to turn off Protected Mode. If you disable this policy setting, Protected Mode will be turned off. It will revert to Internet Explorer 6 behavior that allows for Internet Explorer to write to the registry and the file system. Users will not be able to turn on Protected Mode. If you do not configure this policy, users will be able to turn on or off Protected Mode.","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D45754ED-6BF7-1014-9145-92E53AEC44E5","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223093","mitigations":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:480","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI485-IE11","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Turn On Protected Mode)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:48000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Turn On Protected Mode\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:48000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Turn On Protected Mode\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '2500'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:48000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Turn On Protected Mode\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '2500'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223093r961131_rule","rule_title":"Protected Mode must be enforced (Internet zone).","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Turn on Protected Mode' to 'Enabled', and select 'Enable' from the drop-down box.   ","classification":"Unclassified"},{"comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001084"],"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223094r961131","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000233","documentable":"false","group_id":"V-223094","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Turn on Protected Mode' must be 'Enabled', and 'Enable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"2500\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000233","id":"V-223094"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59549","V-46685"],"discussion":"Protected Mode protects Internet Explorer from exploited vulnerabilities by reducing the locations Internet Explorer can write to in the registry and the file system. If you enable this policy setting, Protected Mode will be turned on. Users will not be able to turn off Protected Mode. If you disable this policy setting, Protected Mode will be turned off. It will revert to Internet Explorer 6 behavior that allows for Internet Explorer to write to the registry and the file system. Users will not be able to turn on Protected Mode. If you do not configure this policy, users will be able to turn on or off Protected Mode.","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4575CC1-6BF7-1014-98D6-F92CF70CFEDC","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223094","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:481"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI490-IE11","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Turn On Protected Mode)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:48100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Turn On Protected Mode\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:48100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Turn On Protected Mode\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '2500'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie: