ame' must be equal to '1809'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:48300 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Use Pop-up Blocker\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '1809'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223096r960963_rule","rule_id":"SV-223096r960963","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59555","V-46691"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Use Pop-up Blocker' must be 'Enabled', and 'Enable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"1809\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"id":"V-223096","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"discussion":"This policy setting allows you to manage whether unwanted pop-up windows appear. Pop-up windows that are opened when the end user clicks a link are not blocked. If you enable this policy setting, most unwanted pop-up windows are prevented from appearing. If you disable this policy setting, pop-up windows are not prevented from appearing. If you do not configure this policy setting, most unwanted pop-up windows are prevented from appearing.","security_override_guidance":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223096"},{"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:484","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI515-IE11","ia_controls":"","uuid":"D457784C-6BF7-1014-8A7A-C5198994AF6A","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-223097","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Web sites in less privileged Web content zones can navigate into this zone' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","rule_title":"Websites in less privileged web content zones must be prevented from navigating into the Internet zone.","classification":"Unclassified","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Web sites in less privileged Web content zones can navigate into this zone)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:48400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Web sites in less privileged Web content zones can navigate into this zone\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:48400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Web sites in less privileged Web content zones can navigate into this zone\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '2101'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:48400 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Internet Zone\\Web sites in less privileged Web content zones can navigate into this zone\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3'\n                        : name equals '2101'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_id_src":"SV-223097r1117169_rule","mitigation_control":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223097r1117169","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-001414"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59557","V-46693"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Internet Zone -&gt; 'Web sites in less privileged Web content zones can navigate into this zone' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\3 Criteria: If the value \"2101\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000039","id":"V-223097"},"discussion":"This policy setting allows a user to manage whether websites from less privileged zones, such as Restricted Sites, can navigate into the Internet zone. If this policy setting is enabled, websites from less privileged zones can open new windows in, or navigate into, this zone. The security zone will run without the added layer of security that is provided by the Protection from Zone Elevation security feature. If \"Prompt\" is selected in the drop-down box, a warning is issued to the user that potentially risky navigation is about to occur. If this policy setting is disabled, the potentially risky navigation is prevented. The Internet Explorer security feature will be on in this zone as set by the Protection from Zone Elevation feature control. If this policy setting is not configured, websites from less privileged zones can open new windows in, or navigate into, this zone.","security_override_guidance":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000039","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223097"},{"potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D457815B-6BF7-1014-B44A-9CE00D783BBB","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223098","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:485","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI520-IE11","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Web sites in less privileged Web content zones can navigate into this zone)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:48500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Web sites in less privileged Web content zones can navigate into this zone\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:48500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Web sites in less privileged Web content zones can navigate into this zone\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '2101'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:48500 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Web sites in less privileged Web content zones can navigate into this zone\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '2101'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223098r1117169_rule","rule_title":"Websites in less privileged web content zones must be prevented from navigating into the Restricted Sites zone.","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Web sites in less privileged Web content zones can navigate into this zone' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001414"],"responsibility":"","rule_id":"SV-223098r1117169","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000039","group_id":"V-223098","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_tree":{"id":"V-223098","title":"SRG-APP-000039"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Web sites in less privileged Web content zones can navigate into this zone' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"2101\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59559","V-46695"],"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"This policy setting allows you to manage whether websites from less privileged zones, such as Restricted Sites, can navigate into the Restricted zone. If this policy setting is enabled, websites from less privileged zones can open new windows in, or navigate into, this zone. The security zone will run without the added layer of security that is provided by the Protection from Zone Elevation security feature. If Prompt is selected in the drop-down box, a warning is issued to the user that potentially risky navigation is about to occur. If this policy setting is disabled, the potentially risky navigation is prevented. The Internet Explorer security feature will be on in this zone as set by the Protection from Zone Elevation feature control. If this policy setting is not configured, websites from less privileged zones can open new windows in, or navigate into, this zone."},{"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI575-IE11","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:486","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223099","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4578A15-6BF7-1014-9310-BBF9D796CCC1","classification":"Unclassified","rule_title":"Allow binary and script behaviors must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow binary and script behaviors' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box. ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_id_src":"SV-223099r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow binary and script behaviors)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:48600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow binary and script behaviors\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:48600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow binary and script behaviors\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '2000'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:48600 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Network\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Allow binary and script behaviors\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '2000'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223099r960963","responsibility":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"discussion":"This policy setting allows you to manage dynamic binary and script behaviors of components that encapsulate specific functionality for HTML elements, to which they were attached. If you enable this policy setting, binary and script behaviors are available.   If you select \"Administrator approved\" in the drop-down box, only the behaviors listed in the Admin-approved Behaviors under Binary Behaviors Security Restriction policy are available.    If you disable this policy setting, binary and script behaviors are not available unless applications have implemented a custom security manager. If you do not configure this policy setting, binary and script behaviors are available.","security_override_guidance":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223099"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Allow binary and script behaviors' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"2000\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59565","V-46701"],"group_id":"V-223099","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141"},{"uuid":"D4579262-6BF7-1014-9C0C-E6B528774141","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","group_id_src":"V-223100","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:487","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI580-IE11","ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Automatic prompting for file downloads)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:48700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Automatic prompting for file downloads\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:48700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Automatic prompting for file downloads\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '2200'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:48700 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Internet Control Panel\\Security Page\\Restricted Sites Zone\\Automatic prompting for file downloads\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4'\n                        : name equals '2200'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_id_src":"SV-223100r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Automatic prompting for file downloads' to 'Enabled', and select 'Disable' from the drop-down box.   ","rule_title":"Automatic prompting for file downloads must be disallowed (Restricted Sites zone).","classification":"Unclassified","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","rule_id":"SV-223100r960963","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223100","legacy_ids":["SV-59569","V-46705"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223100"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Internet Control Panel -&gt; Security Page -&gt; Restricted Sites Zone -&gt; 'Automatic prompting for file downloads' must be 'Enabled', and 'Disable' selected from the drop-down box. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\Zones\\4 Criteria: If the value \"2200\" is REG_DWORD = 3, this is not a finding.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"This policy setting determines whether users will be prompted for non user-initiated file downloads. Regardless of this setting, users will receive file download dialogs for user-initiated downloads. Users may accept downloads that they did not request, and those downloaded files may include malicious code. If you enable this setting, users will receive a file download dialog for automatic download attempts. If you disable or do not configure this setting, file downloads that are not user-initiated will be blocked, and users will see the information bar instead of the file download dialog. Users can then click the information bar to allow the file download prompt."},{"false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223101r961083","severity":"medium","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001166"],"responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-223101","title":"SRG-APP-000206"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Consistent Mime Handling -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_HANDLING Criteria: If the value \"(Reserved)\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59573","V-46709"],"discussion":"Internet Explorer uses Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions (MIME) data to determine file handling procedures for files received through a web server. The Consistent MIME Handling\\Internet Explorer Processes policy setting determines whether Internet Explorer requires all file-type information provided by web servers to be consistent. For example, if the MIME type of a file is text/plain but the MIME data indicates the file is really an executable file, Internet Explorer changes its extension to reflect this executable status. This capability helps ensure executable code cannot masquerade as other types of data that may be trusted. If you enable this policy setting, Internet Explorer examines all received files and enforces consistent MIME data for them. If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, Internet Explorer does not require consistent MIME data for all received files and will use the MIME data provided by the file. MIME file-type spoofing is a potential threat to an organization. Ensuring these files are consistent and properly labeled helps prevent malicious file downloads from infecting your network.","security_override_guidance":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000206","documentable":"false","group_id":"V-223101","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:488"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI590-IE11","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D4579AC7-6BF7-1014-A35E-FB13DEE7D327","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223101","status":"not_a_finding","rule_title":"Internet Explorer Processes for MIME handling must be enforced. (Reserved)","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Consistent Mime Handling -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' to 'Enabled'.  ","reference_identifier":"4095","classification":"Unclassified","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Consistent Mime Handling\\Internet Explorer Processes)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:48800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Consistent Mime Handling\\Internet Explorer Processes\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:48800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Consistent Mime Handling\\Internet Explorer Processes\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_HANDLING'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '(Reserved)'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:48800 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Consistent Mime Handling\\Internet Explorer Processes\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_HANDLING'\n                        : name equals '(Reserved)'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223101r961083_rule"},{"uuid":"D457A354-6BF7-1014-B00C-F215162DEE3F","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223102","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:502","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI592-IE11","ia_controls":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Consistent Mime Handling\\Internet Explorer Processes)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:50200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Consistent Mime Handling\\Internet Explorer Processes\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:50200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Consistent Mime Handling\\Internet Explorer Processes\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_HANDLING'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'explorer.exe'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:50200 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Consistent Mime Handling\\Internet Explorer Processes\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_HANDLING'\n                        : name equals 'explorer.exe'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223102r961083_rule","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Consistent Mime Handling -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' to 'Enabled'.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","rule_title":"Internet Explorer Processes for MIME handling must be enforced (Explorer).","classification":"Unclassified","ccis":["CCI-001166"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223102r961083","severity":"medium","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000206","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223102","legacy_ids":["SV-59575","V-46711"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000206","id":"V-223102"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Consistent Mime Handling -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_HANDLING Criteria: If the value \"explorer.exe\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Internet Explorer uses Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions (MIME) data to determine file handling procedures for files received through a web server. The Consistent MIME Handling\\Internet Explorer Processes policy setting determines whether Internet Explorer requires all file-type information provided by web servers to be consistent. For example, if the MIME type of a file is text/plain but the MIME data indicates the file is really an executable file, Internet Explorer changes its extension to reflect this executable status. This capability helps ensure executable code cannot masquerade as other types of data that may be trusted. If you enable this policy setting, Internet Explorer examines all received files and enforces consistent MIME data for them. If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, Internet Explorer does not require consistent MIME data for all received files and will use the MIME data provided by the file. MIME file-type spoofing is a potential threat to the organization. Ensuring these files are consistent and properly labeled helps prevent malicious file downloads from infecting the network. This guide recommends configuring this policy as \"Enabled\" for all environments specified in this guide."},{"documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000206","group_id":"V-223103","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Consistent Mime Handling -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_HANDLING Criteria: If the value \"iexplore.exe\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"id":"V-223103","title":"SRG-APP-000206"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59577","V-46713"],"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Internet Explorer uses Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions (MIME) data to determine file handling procedures for files received through a web server. The Consistent MIME Handling\\Internet Explorer Processes policy setting determines whether Internet Explorer requires all file-type information provided by web servers to be consistent. For example, if the MIME type of a file is text/plain but the MIME data indicates that the file is really an executable file, Internet Explorer changes its extension to reflect this executable status. This capability helps ensure that executable code cannot masquerade as other types of data that may be trusted. If you enable this policy setting, Internet Explorer examines all received files and enforces consistent MIME data for them. If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, Internet Explorer does not require consistent MIME data for all received files and will use the MIME data provided by the file. MIME file-type spoofing is a potential threat to an organization. Ensuring these files are consistent and properly labeled helps prevent malicious file downloads from infecting the network. This guide recommends configuring this policy as \"Enabled\" for all environments specified in this guide.","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001166"],"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223103r961083","severity":"medium","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Consistent Mime Handling\\Internet Explorer Processes)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:50300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Consistent Mime Handling\\Internet Explorer Processes\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:50300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Consistent Mime Handling\\Internet Explorer Processes\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_HANDLING'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'iexplore.exe'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:50300 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Consistent Mime Handling\\Internet Explorer Processes\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_HANDLING'\n                        : name equals 'iexplore.exe'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223103r961083_rule","rule_title":"Internet Explorer Processes for MIME handling must be enforced (iexplore).","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Consistent Mime Handling -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' to 'Enabled'.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","classification":"Unclassified","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D457ABAF-6BF7-1014-85C1-EDCC45F3D237","status":"not_a_finding","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223103","weight":"10.0","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:503"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI594-IE11"},{"group_id":"V-223104","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000206","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"MIME sniffing is the process of examining the content of a MIME file to determine its context - whether it is a data file, an executable file, or some other type of file. This policy setting determines whether Internet Explorer MIME sniffing will prevent promotion of a file of one type to a more dangerous file type. When set to \"Enabled\", MIME sniffing will never promote a file of one type to a more dangerous file type. Disabling MIME sniffing configures Internet Explorer processes to allow a MIME sniff that promotes a file of one type to a more dangerous file type. For example, promoting a text file to an executable file is a dangerous promotion because any code in the supposed text file would be executed. MIME file-type spoofing is a potential threat to an organization. Ensuring these files are consistently handled helps prevent malicious file downloads from infecting the network. This guide recommends you configure this policy as \"Enabled\" for all environments specified in this guide. Note: This setting works in conjunction with, but does not replace, the Consistent MIME Handling settings.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000206","id":"V-223104"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Mime Sniffing Safety Feature -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_SNIFFING Criteria: If the value \"(Reserved)\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59579","V-46715"],"responsibility":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001166"],"severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223104r961083","rule_id_src":"SV-223104r961083_rule","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Mime Sniffing Safety Feature\\Internet Explorer Processes)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:48900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Mime Sniffing Safety Feature\\Internet Explorer Processes\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:48900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Mime Sniffing Safety Feature\\Internet Explorer Processes\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_SNIFFING'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '(Reserved)'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:48900 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Mime Sniffing Safety Feature\\Internet Explorer Processes\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_SNIFFING'\n                        : name equals '(Reserved)'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","classification":"Unclassified","rule_title":"Internet Explorer Processes for MIME sniffing must be enforced (Reserved).","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Mime Sniffing Safety Feature -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' to 'Enabled'.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223104","mitigations":"","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D457B3B0-6BF7-1014-A652-ADF62B0D9C67","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI595-IE11","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:489","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"}},{"discussion":"MIME sniffing is the process of examining the content of a MIME file to determine its context - whether it is a data file, an executable file, or some other type of file. This policy setting determines whether Internet Explorer MIME sniffing will prevent promotion of a file of one type to a more dangerous file type. When set to \"Enabled\", MIME sniffing will never promote a file of one type to a more dangerous file type. Disabling MIME sniffing configures Internet Explorer processes to allow a MIME sniff that promotes a file of one type to a more dangerous file type. For example, promoting a text file to an executable file is a dangerous promotion because any code in the supposed text file would be executed. MIME file-type spoofing is a potential threat to an organization. Ensuring these files are consistently handled helps prevent malicious file downloads from infecting the network. This guide recommends configuring this policy as \"Enabled\" for all environments specified in this guide. Note: This setting works in conjunction with, but does not replace, the Consistent MIME Handling settings.","security_override_guidance":"","check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Mime Sniffing Safety Feature -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_SNIFFING Criteria: If the value \"explorer.exe\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000206","id":"V-223105"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59581","V-46717"],"group_id":"V-223105","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_title":"SRG-APP-000206","documentable":"false","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223105r961083","responsibility":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001166"],"classification":"Unclassified","rule_title":"Internet Explorer Processes for MIME sniffing must be enforced (Explorer).","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Mime Sniffing Safety Feature -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' to 'Enabled'.  ","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223105r961083_rule","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Mime Sniffing Safety Feature\\Internet Explorer Processes must be Enabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:51000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Mime Sniffing Safety Feature\\Internet Explorer Processes must be Enabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:51000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Mime Sniffing Safety Feature\\Internet Explorer Processes must be Enabled\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_SNIFFING'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'explorer.exe'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:51000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Mime Sniffing Safety Feature\\Internet Explorer Processes must be Enabled\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_SNIFFING'\n                        : name equals 'explorer.exe'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI596-IE11","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:510","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223105","status":"not_a_finding","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D457BB70-6BF7-1014-A0C4-FAE89C021317"},{"rule_version":"DTBI597-IE11","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:511","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"group_id_src":"V-223106","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"D457CC85-6BF7-1014-9970-F74DA937CCE5","potential_impacts":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Mime Sniffing Safety Feature -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' to 'Enabled'.   ","rule_title":"Internet Explorer Processes for MIME sniffing must be enforced (iexplore).","rule_id_src":"SV-223106r961083_rule","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Mime Sniffing Safety Feature\\Internet Explorer Processes must be Enabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:51100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Mime Sniffing Safety Feature\\Internet Explorer Processes must be Enabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:51100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Mime Sniffing Safety Feature\\Internet Explorer Processes must be Enabled\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_SNIFFING'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'iexplore.exe'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:51100 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Mime Sniffing Safety Feature\\Internet Explorer Processes must be Enabled\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_SNIFFING'\n                        : name equals 'iexplore.exe'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","severity":"medium","rule_id":"SV-223106r961083","false_positives":"","responsibility":"","ccis":["CCI-001166"],"comments":null,"discussion":"MIME sniffing is the process of examining the content of a MIME file to determine its context - whether it is a data file, an executable file, or some other type of file. This policy setting determines whether Internet Explorer MIME sniffing will prevent promotion of a file of one type to a more dangerous file type. When set to \"Enabled\", MIME sniffing will never promote a file of one type to a more dangerous file type. Disabling MIME sniffing configures Internet Explorer processes to allow a MIME sniff that promotes a file of one type to a more dangerous file type. For example, promoting a text file to an executable file is a dangerous promotion because any code in the supposed text file would be executed. MIME file-type spoofing is a potential threat to an organization. Ensuring these files are consistently handled helps prevent malicious file downloads from infecting the network. This guide recommends configuring this policy as \"Enabled\" for all environments specified in this guide. Note: This setting works in conjunction with, but does not replace, the Consistent MIME Handling settings.","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59583","V-46719"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Mime Sniffing Safety Feature -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_MIME_SNIFFING Criteria: If the value \"iexplore.exe\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000206","id":"V-223106"},"stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223106","group_title":"SRG-APP-000206","documentable":"false"},{"documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223107","legacy_ids":["SV-59585","V-46721"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-223107","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; MK Protocol Security Restriction -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_DISABLE_MK_PROTOCOL Criteria: If the value \"(Reserved)\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","discussion":"The MK Protocol Security Restriction policy setting reduces attack surface area by blocking the seldom used MK protocol. Some older web applications use the MK protocol to retrieve information from compressed files. Because the MK protocol is not widely used, it should be blocked wherever it is not needed. Setting this policy to \"Enabled\"; blocks the MK protocol for Windows Explorer and Internet Explorer, which causes resources that use the MK protocol to fail. Disabling this setting allows applications to use the MK protocol API. This guide recommends configuring this setting to \"Enabled\" to block the MK protocol unless it is specifically needed in the environment. Note: Because resources that use the MK protocol will fail when deploying this setting, ensure none of the applications use the MK protocol.","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223107r960963","severity":"medium","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\MK Protocol Security Restriction\\Internet Explorer Processes)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:50400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\MK Protocol Security Restriction\\Internet Explorer Processes\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:50400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\MK Protocol Security Restriction\\Internet Explorer Processes\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_DISABLE_MK_PROTOCOL'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '(Reserved)'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:50400 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\MK Protocol Security Restriction\\Internet Explorer Processes\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_DISABLE_MK_PROTOCOL'\n                        : name equals '(Reserved)'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223107r960963_rule","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; MK Protocol Security Restriction -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' to 'Enabled'.   ","rule_title":"Internet Explorer Processes for MK protocol must be enforced (Reserved).","classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"D457D58B-6BF7-1014-8214-E70AE7ACC808","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-223107","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:504"},"rule_version":"DTBI599-IE11","ia_controls":""},{"uuid":"D457DD90-6BF7-1014-B022-980D78012750","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-223108","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:490"},"rule_version":"DTBI600-IE11","ia_controls":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\MK Protocol Security Restriction\\Internet Explorer Processes)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:49000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\MK Protocol Security Restriction\\Internet Explorer Processes\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:49000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\MK Protocol Security Restriction\\Internet Explorer Processes\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_DISABLE_MK_PROTOCOL'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'explorer.exe'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:49000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\MK Protocol Security Restriction\\Internet Explorer Processes\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_DISABLE_MK_PROTOCOL'\n                        : name equals 'explorer.exe'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223108r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; MK Protocol Security Restriction -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' to 'Enabled'.   ","rule_title":"Internet Explorer Processes for MK protocol must be enforced (Explorer).","classification":"Unclassified","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","rule_id":"SV-223108r960963","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223108","legacy_ids":["SV-59587","V-46723"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223108"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; MK Protocol Security Restriction -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_DISABLE_MK_PROTOCOL Criteria: If the value \"explorer.exe\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","discussion":"The MK Protocol Security Restriction policy setting reduces attack surface area by blocking the seldom used MK protocol. Some older web applications use the MK protocol to retrieve information from compressed files. Because the MK protocol is not widely used, it should be blocked wherever it is not needed. Setting this policy to \"Enabled\"; blocks the MK protocol for Windows Explorer and Internet Explorer, which causes resources that use the MK protocol to fail. Disabling this setting allows applications to use the MK protocol API. This guide recommends you configure this setting to \"Enabled\" to block the MK protocol unless it is specifically needed in the environment. Note: Because resources that use the MK protocol will fail when deploying this setting, ensure none of the applications use the MK protocol.","security_override_guidance":""},{"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:491","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"DTBI605-IE11","ia_controls":"","uuid":"D457E5B3-6BF7-1014-8E3A-95BC4A9F3C08","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223109","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; MK Protocol Security Restriction -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' to 'Enabled'. ","rule_title":"Internet Explorer Processes for MK protocol must be enforced (iexplore).","classification":"Unclassified","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\MK Protocol Security Restriction\\Internet Explorer Processes)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:49100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\MK Protocol Security Restriction\\Internet Explorer Processes\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:49100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\MK Protocol Security Restriction\\Internet Explorer Processes\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_DISABLE_MK_PROTOCOL'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'iexplore.exe'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:49100 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\MK Protocol Security Restriction\\Internet Explorer Processes\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_DISABLE_MK_PROTOCOL'\n                        : name equals 'iexplore.exe'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_id_src":"SV-223109r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223109r960963","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","legacy_ids":["SV-59589","V-46725"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223109"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; MK Protocol Security Restriction -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_DISABLE_MK_PROTOCOL Criteria: If the value \"iexplore.exe\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"The MK Protocol Security Restriction policy setting reduces attack surface area by blocking the seldom used MK protocol. Some older web applications use the MK protocol to retrieve information from compressed files. Because the MK protocol is not widely used, it should be blocked wherever it is not needed. Setting this policy to \"Enabled\"; blocks the MK protocol for Windows Explorer and Internet Explorer, which causes resources that use the MK protocol to fail. Disabling this setting allows applications to use the MK protocol API. This guide recommends you configure this setting to \"Enabled\" to block the MK protocol unless specifically needed in the environment. Note: Because resources that use the MK protocol will fail when deploying this setting, ensure none of the applications use the MK protocol.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223109"},{"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:492","href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI610-IE11","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D457EDC3-6BF7-1014-9A9D-FF967E8DF25B","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-223110","mitigations":"","rule_title":"Internet Explorer Processes for Zone Elevation must be enforced (Reserved).","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Protection From Zone Elevation -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' to 'Enabled'.   ","reference_identifier":"4095","classification":"Unclassified","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Protection From Zone Elevation\\Internet Explorer Processes)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:49200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Protection From Zone Elevation\\Internet Explorer Processes\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:49200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Protection From Zone Elevation\\Internet Explorer Processes\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_ZONE_ELEVATION'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '(Reserved)'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:49200 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Protection From Zone Elevation\\Internet Explorer Processes\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_ZONE_ELEVATION'\n                        : name equals '(Reserved)'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223110r961131_rule","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223110r961131","severity":"medium","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001084"],"responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-223110","title":"SRG-APP-000233"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Protection From Zone Elevation -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' must be 'Enabled'.  Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_ZONE_ELEVATION Criteria: If the value \"(Reserved)\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59591","V-46727"],"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Internet Explorer places restrictions on each web page it opens that are dependent upon the location of the web page (such as Internet Zone, Intranet Zone, or Local Machine Zone). Web pages on a local computer have the fewest security restrictions and reside in the Local Machine Zone, which makes the Local Machine Security Zone a prime target for malicious attackers. If you enable this policy setting, any zone can be protected from zone elevation by Internet Explorer processes. This approach stops content running in one zone from gaining the elevated privileges of another zone. If you disable this policy setting, no zone receives such protection from Internet Explorer processes. Because of the severity and relative frequency of zone elevation attacks, this guide recommends that you configure this setting as \"Enabled\" in all environments.","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000233","group_id":"V-223110","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D"},{"group_title":"SRG-APP-000233","documentable":"false","group_id":"V-223111","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000233","id":"V-223111"},"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Protection From Zone Elevation -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_ZONE_ELEVATION Criteria: If the value \"explorer.exe\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","legacy_ids":["SV-59593","V-46729"],"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Internet Explorer places restrictions on each web page it opens that are dependent upon the location of the web page (such as Internet Zone, Intranet Zone, or Local Machine Zone). Web pages on a local computer have the fewest security restrictions and reside in the Local Machine Zone, which makes the Local Machine Security Zone a prime target for malicious attackers. If you enable this policy setting, any zone can be protected from zone elevation by Internet Explorer processes. This approach stops content running in one zone from gaining the elevated privileges of another zone. If you disable this policy setting, no zone receives such protection from Internet Explorer processes. Because of the severity and relative frequency of zone elevation attacks, this guide recommends configuring this setting as \"Enabled\" in all environments.","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001084"],"responsibility":"","rule_id":"SV-223111r961131","false_positives":"","severity":"medium","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Protection From Zone Elevation\\Internet Explorer Processes)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:50500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Protection From Zone Elevation\\Internet Explorer Processes\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:50500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Protection From Zone Elevation\\Internet Explorer Processes\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_ZONE_ELEVATION'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'explorer.exe'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:50500 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Protection From Zone Elevation\\Internet Explorer Processes\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_ZONE_ELEVATION'\n                        : name equals 'explorer.exe'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_id_src":"SV-223111r961131_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Internet Explorer Processes for Zone Elevation must be enforced (Explorer).","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Protection From Zone Elevation -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' to 'Enabled'.   ","classification":"Unclassified","potential_impacts":"","uuid":"D457F5D8-6BF7-1014-A31E-D38CCA89C63E","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223111","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:505"},"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI612-IE11"},{"ccis":["CCI-001084"],"comments":null,"responsibility":"","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223112r961131","severity":"medium","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-APP-000233","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_id":"V-223112","legacy_ids":["SV-59595","V-46731"],"check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Protection From Zone Elevation -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_ZONE_ELEVATION Criteria: If the value \"iexplore.exe\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000233","id":"V-223112"},"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Internet Explorer places restrictions on each web page it opens that are dependent upon the location of the web page (such as Internet Zone, Intranet Zone, or Local Machine Zone). Web pages on a local computer have the fewest security restrictions and reside in the Local Machine Zone, which makes the Local Machine Security Zone a prime target for malicious attackers. If you enable this policy setting, any zone can be protected from zone elevation by Internet Explorer processes. This approach stops content running in one zone from gaining the elevated privileges of another zone. If you disable this policy setting, no zone receives such protection from Internet Explorer processes. Because of the severity and relative frequency of zone elevation attacks, this guide recommends that you configure this setting as \"Enabled\" in all environments.","uuid":"D457FDC3-6BF7-1014-9B8D-C63FAD73E2EB","potential_impacts":"","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","group_id_src":"V-223112","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV16-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:def:506"},"rule_version":"DTBI614-IE11","ia_controls":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Protection From Zone Elevation\\Internet Explorer Processes)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:50600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Protection From Zone Elevation\\Internet Explorer Processes\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:50600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Protection From Zone Elevation\\Internet Explorer Processes\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_ZONE_ELEVATION'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'iexplore.exe'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:50600 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Protection From Zone Elevation\\Internet Explorer Processes\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_ZONE_ELEVATION'\n                        : name equals 'iexplore.exe'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-223112r961131_rule","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Protection From Zone Elevation -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' to 'Enabled'.   ","rule_title":"Internet Explorer Processes for Zone Elevation must be enforced (iexplore).","classification":"Unclassified"},{"security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"In certain circumstances, websites can initiate file download prompts without interaction from users. This technique can allow websites to put unauthorized files on users' hard drives if they click the wrong button and accept the download. If you configure the Restrict File Download\\Internet Explorer Processes policy setting to \"Enabled\", file download prompts that are not user-initiated are blocked for Internet Explorer processes. If you configure this policy setting as \"Disabled\", prompting will occur for file downloads that are not user-initiated for Internet Explorer processes. Note: This setting is configured as \"Enabled\" in all environments specified in this guide to help prevent attackers from placing arbitrary code on users' computers.","check_content":"The policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Restrict File Download -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' must be 'Enabled'. Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_RESTRICT_FILEDOWNLOAD Criteria: If the value \"(Reserved)\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-223113"},"legacy_ids":["SV-59597","V-46733"],"group_id":"V-223113","stig_uuid":"D437A425-6BF7-1014-8C79-A5C858995E8D","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","documentable":"false","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-223113r960963","responsibility":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"classification":"Unclassified","rule_title":"Internet Explorer Processes for Restrict File Download must be enforced (Reserved).","reference_identifier":"4095","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Windows Components -&gt; Internet Explorer -&gt; Security Features -&gt; Restrict File Download -&gt; 'Internet Explorer Processes' to 'Enabled'.   ","rule_id_src":"SV-223113r960963_rule","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:55\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\ Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Restrict File Download\\Internet Explorer Processes)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:tst:49300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\ Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Restrict File Download\\Internet Explorer Processes\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:obj:49300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\ Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Restrict File Download\\Internet Explorer Processes\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_RESTRICT_FILEDOWNLOAD'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '(Reserved)'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.ie:ste:49300 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\ Internet Explorer\\Security Features\\Restrict File Download\\Internet Explorer Processes\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main\\FeatureControl\\FEATURE_RESTRICT_FILEDOWNLOAD'\n                        : name equals '(Reserved)'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","third_party_tools":"","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"DTBI630-IE11","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IE11_V2R9_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-e